#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2
msgid "Alert analysis module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3
msgid ""
"*Monitor forest cover loss alerts in an area of interest, period after "
"period*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:7
msgid ""
"**Alert analysis module** is a SEPAL app for monitoring forest cover loss"
" in an area of interest (AOI). The app:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:9
msgid ""
"downloads the Global Land Analysis and Discovery (GLAD) alerts GLAD-L and"
" GLAD-S2 and the Radar for Detecting Deforestation (RADD) alerts from "
"Google Earth Engine (GEE), and your own alert sources if you have them;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:10
msgid "aligns them on one grid;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:11
msgid ""
"groups touching alert pixels into alerts, each listing every source that "
"flagged it; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:12
msgid ""
"lets you review the alerts one by one on *before* and *after* satellite "
"images."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:14
msgid ""
"For each alert, confirm or reject it, answer your own questions about it,"
" and redraw its polygon by hand or with two neural-network models. The "
"review can be split among several evaluators. The results come out as "
"GeoPackage files, comma-separated values (CSV) tables, Word reports and "
"animated GIF images."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:16
msgid ""
"This article is for forest-monitoring analysts who use SEPAL. It "
"describes each step of the app, in the order of use, and ends with a "
"worked example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:21
msgid "Workflow at a glance"
msgstr ""

