#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:93
msgid "The launching process can take several minutes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:98
msgid "The app window"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:100
msgid ""
"The map fills the window. The **Workflow** panel on the right side holds "
"the steps. A narrow rail of icons runs down the left side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:102
msgid ""
"The header of the **Workflow** panel stays in view while the step under "
"it scrolls:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:104
msgid ""
"One title row shows the step's position among all the steps (e.g. \"3 / "
"8\"), its name and what it holds (\"3 sources\"). An optional step that "
"is still empty shows no count. The arrows on each side go to the step "
"before or after."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:105
msgid ""
"Select the name to open the list of steps, grouped under the two levels, "
"**Prepare alerts** and **Set up review**. Each step has a numbered dot: "
"filled when the step has outputs (an AOI, periods, sources…), a grey ring"
" when it is still empty. The two optional steps, **Additional layers** "
"and **Questionnaire**, have a dashed dot. A locked step is greyed out and"
" says why (e.g. \"Build an alert set first.\"). A level's name gets a "
"check mark once its last required step has outputs. Select a step to open"
" it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:106
msgid ""
"Under the name, one line says what to do in the step (e.g. \"Set the "
"monitoring period.\"). The information button at the right side of that "
"line opens the step's help."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:108
msgid ""
"At the bottom of the panel, **Back** and **Next** go to the step before "
"or after, skipping locked steps. Hover over one to see the name of the "
"step it opens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:110
msgid "To use the left rail:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:112
msgid "Hover over an icon to view its name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:113
msgid ""
"Select the arrow on the edge of the rail to expand it and show the names."
" Select its pin to keep it expanded. An expanded rail that is not pinned "
"folds back when you click on the map, on the main screen as on the "
"Analysis maps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:117
msgid ""
"While a dialog is open, the rail does not respond. Close the dialog with "
"its cross first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:119
msgid "From top to bottom, the rail holds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:121
msgid "**Map**: shows the map with no dialog over it;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:122
msgid ""
"**About**: a short description of the app (the sources it downloads, how "
"the alerts are reviewed and exported, and where your projects are saved);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:123
msgid "**Project**: opens the `Project <defo-project_>`_ dialog;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:124
msgid "**Analysis**: opens the `Analysis <defo-analysis_>`_ screen; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:125
msgid "**Overview**: opens the `Overview <defo-overview_>`_ dialog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:127
msgid ""
"At the bottom of the rail are three links to the app's GitHub repository "
"(its source code, its documentation and a form to report a bug), then two"
" buttons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:129
msgid ""
"The theme button switches, at each click, between the dark theme (moon "
"icon), the light theme (sun icon) and an automatic theme that follows "
"your system's setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:130
msgid ""
"The language selector shows the code of the current language. Select it "
"to choose English, Spanish, French or Portuguese. The app's labels change"
" at once. At first, the app follows the browser's language when it is one"
" of these four, and English otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:132
msgid "The browser remembers the theme and the language for the next session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:137
msgid "Project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:139
msgid ""
"All work happens inside a *project*: one AOI, its alert sources, its "
"monitoring periods and every alert set built from them. A project is a "
"folder in your SEPAL home. The app saves it automatically after every "
"change: there is no **Save** button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:141
msgid ""
"Use the **Project** dialog to create, open, import, copy and delete "
"projects. It opens by itself when the app starts. Afterwards, select "
"**Project** in the left rail."
msgstr ""

