msgid ""
"Enter text in the **Search projects** field to keep only the projects "
"whose name contains it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:228
msgid "Select a project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:229
msgid "Select **Open**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:231
msgid "To rename a project:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:233
msgid ""
"Select the pencil icon on its row (or next to the name of the open "
"project)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:234
msgid "Enter the new name. It follows the same rules as a new project's name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:235
msgid "Select **Rename**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:237
msgid "A project cannot be renamed while a task is still writing into it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:239
msgid "To delete a project:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:241
msgid ""
"Select the red bin icon on its row. The confirmation dialog shows the "
"size of the project folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:242
msgid "Enter the project's name exactly in the confirmation field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:243
msgid "Select **Delete**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:247
msgid ""
"Deleting removes the whole project folder: downloads, alert sets, reviews"
" and reports. It cannot be undone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:249
msgid "Deleting the open project closes it first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:250
msgid ""
"A project cannot be deleted while a task (a download, an **Integrate & "
"vectorize** run or a review save) is still writing into it. Wait for the "
"task to end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:255
msgid "Duplicate a project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:257
msgid ""
"**Duplicate** copies the open project under a new name. The copy keeps "
"the AOI, sources, masks, layers and grid, the look-back and the report "
"template, without periods or alert sets. The copy opens on its AOI step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:259
msgid "Use it to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:261
msgid "start a new monitoring round from the same setup; or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:262
msgid ""
"monitor another area once the AOI of a project is locked (see `Area of "
"interest <defo-aoi_>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:264
msgid "**Duplicate** is not offered for a review copy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:269
msgid "Import a review package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:271
msgid ""
"When a project's creator splits the alerts among several evaluators (see "
"`Evaluation <defo-evaluation_>`_), each evaluator receives a *review "
"package*: one .zip file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:273
msgid "To work on a review package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:275
msgid "Copy the .zip file into your SEPAL folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:276
msgid "In the **Project** dialog, select **Import**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:277
msgid ""
"In the **Import a review package** dialog, select the file in **Review "
"package (.zip)**. The import starts as soon as the file is selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:279
msgid ""
"The package becomes a new project, a *review copy*, named after the "
"original project and the evaluator (e.g. ``madre-de-dios__e01-ana``). It "
"opens directly on the `Analysis <defo-analysis_>`_ screen, filtered to "
"the alerts assigned to that evaluator. In a review copy the setup steps "
"are locked, and a banner reads: \"Review copy for (evaluator), from "
"(project). Setup is locked.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:281
msgid ""
"If the same package was already imported, the **Already imported** dialog"
" offers two options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:283
msgid "**Open existing copy**: opens the existing copy, with its reviews; or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:284
msgid ""
"**Import as new copy**: imports the package again as a separate project. "
"The existing copy is never overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:288
msgid ""
"A *reviewed copy* (the file an evaluator sends back) cannot be imported "
"here. The project's creator merges it in the `Evaluation <defo-"
"evaluation_>`_ step of the original project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:293
msgid "Open a version 1 recipe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:295
msgid ""
"Recipes saved with the previous version of the app (version 1) stay in "
"their folders under ``module_results/deforestation_alerts/``. **Manage "
"projects** lists them among the projects, marked with a **version 1** "
"chip. Hover over the chip to read: \"Saved with the previous version. It "
"is converted the first time you open it; the old files are kept.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:297
msgid ""
"To open a recipe, select it, then select **Open**, as for a project (or "
"**Continue**, when the dialog offers it). The first time, the app "
"converts it into a project in the same folder: the row reads \"Converting"
" (name)…\" while the app gets the recipe's AOI (from GEE for an "
"administrative area or an asset) and reads its alerts. The project then "
"opens on the `Analysis <defo-analysis_>`_ screen, and the app confirms, "
"e.g. \"recipe_2026-08-12-101500 was converted from version 1. 5 of 40 "
"alerts reviewed.\" Later opens skip the conversion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:299
msgid "The converted project keeps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:301
msgid "the recipe's period, sources and alerts;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:302
msgid ""
"every review: the status, the description, the drawn polygon, the area, "
"the administrative names, the before and after images, and the alert the "
"review stopped at; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:303
msgid ""
"the recipe's mask and extra layer, as the additional layers ``v1 mask`` "
"and ``v1 layer``, and its report template when the file is still there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:305
msgid ""
"The alerts are drawn as rectangles (the boxes version 1 drew around "
"them), with the polygon drawn in a review on top. They keep their version"
" 1 numbers, which start at 0. An alert without a drawn polygon gets an "
"area estimated from its number of alert pixels. When part of the recipe "
"cannot be converted, a warning lists it once, after the conversion (e.g. "
"\"source CCDC: not imported as a source, kept in the alert set only\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:307
msgid ""
"A converted project is locked, and a banner reads: \"This project comes "
"from a version 1 recipe. Only additional layers can be changed; review, "
"save and export work as usual.\" Its AOI, period, sources, Harmonize, "
"Integrate & vectorize, questionnaire and report template cannot change, "
"and it cannot be duplicated. The `Evaluation <defo-evaluation_>`_ step is"
" not available: one person reviews the project. The `Additional layers "
"<defo-layers_>`_ can be added, edited and deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:309
msgid ""
"The recipe's own files (``recipe_parameters.json``, ``alert_db.csv`` and "
"the files made for each alert) are never changed. A recipe cannot be "
"renamed before it is converted: its pencil icon reads \"Open it once to "
"convert it first.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:311
msgid ""
"If the conversion fails, nothing is written, and the message gives the "
"cause, e.g. \"Could not get the area of interest: (error). The recipe was"
" not changed.\""
msgstr ""

