#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:427
msgid ""
"The AOI cannot change while a task is writing into the project (a "
"download or an **Integrate & vectorize** run). The app displays: \"A job "
"is writing into this project; change the AOI once it has finished.\" Wait"
" for the task to end, then select the area again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:432
msgid "Monitoring period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:434
msgid ""
"A *period* is one monitoring round, usually a month. For each period, the"
" app downloads the period's alert sources over its dates plus a *look-"
"back* before them, and builds that period's alert sets. A project usually"
" holds a series of consecutive periods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:436
msgid ""
"Both dates of a period are included: a period from 1 to 31 January keeps "
"the alerts dated on the 1st and on the 31st. The same holds for its "
"search window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:438
msgid ""
"Open the **Period** step of the **Workflow** panel. It unlocks once the "
"project has an `AOI <defo-aoi_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:442
msgid "The Period step with one period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:448
msgid "Loss that spans several periods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:450
msgid ""
"Each period is processed on its own, but forest loss does not keep to the"
" period's dates. Some loss could be missed between two periods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:452
msgid "a clearing that starts too small to be an alert;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:453
msgid ""
"alerts that the providers publish late, after their period was processed;"
" or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:454
msgid ""
"a clearing that keeps growing at the edge of an alert reported in an "
"earlier period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:456
msgid ""
"The app tracks this loss from one period to the next, and never reports "
"the same loss twice:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:462
msgid "Case"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:463
msgid "What the app does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:464
msgid "Loss already reported by an earlier period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:465
msgid ""
"Its pixels (the *footprint* of the earlier alert set) are removed from "
"the new period's run, so it is not reported again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:466
msgid "A cluster too small to be an alert, or an alert published late"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:467
msgid ""
"The `look-back <defo-period-lookback_>`_ searches back into the earlier "
"period: the pixels set aside come back and can join new pixels to form an"
" alert."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:468
msgid "A clearing that grows next to a reviewed alert"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:469
msgid ""
"The new alert is `linked to the earlier alert <defo-period-growth_>`_ as "
"a *growth alert*, and kept even when it is under the minimum size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:474
msgid "The search window and the look-back"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:476
msgid ""
"A clearing often starts small and grows over the following weeks. In the "
"period where it starts, its cluster of alert pixels is still smaller than"
" the **Minimum cluster size** of `Integrate & vectorize <defo-"
"integrate_>`_, so it does not become an alert: its pixels are set aside "
"as *not analysable*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:478
msgid "The look-back keeps these pixels in play:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:480
msgid ""
"Each period searches a wider *search window*: its own dates plus the "
"look-back days before its start."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:481
msgid ""
"The pixels set aside by the earlier period come back into the run and "
"join the new pixels that touch them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:482
msgid ""
"If the cluster they form together reaches the minimum size, it becomes an"
" alert. Its first detection date is the date of its earliest pixel, in "
"the earlier period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:484
msgid ""
"To avoid reporting the same loss twice, every pixel already reported by "
"an alert set of an *earlier* period is removed before the new period's "
"alerts are built: only what was set aside comes back. The look-back also "
"catches alerts that the providers published late, after the earlier "
"period was processed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:486
msgid ""
"The look-back: a cluster too small in one period joins the next period's "
"pixels and becomes an alert, and a reported alert is never reported again"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:491
msgid ""
"The first period has no earlier set to compare with, so every alert in "
"its search window is kept. Its row reads **No earlier set: every alert in"
" the search window is kept**. With a look-back, that includes alerts "
"dated before the period's start."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:493
msgid ""
"A new project's first period starts with no look-back, so it searches "
"only its own dates unless a look-back is set. A project made with "
"**Duplicate** keeps the look-back of the project it was copied from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:498
msgid "Growth next to earlier alerts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:500
msgid ""
"The pixels of a reported alert are part of the footprint, so the look-"
"back does not bring them back. But a clearing often keeps growing at the "
"edge of an alert reported in an earlier period. The new pixels then form "
"a cluster of their own, often smaller than the **Minimum cluster size**, "
"which would be set aside like any small cluster."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:502
msgid ""
"When the earlier alert was saved as **True alert** or **Needs revision**,"
" `Integrate & vectorize <defo-integrate-growth_>`_ keeps this growth in "
"view:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:504
msgid ""
"A new alert that touches the earlier alert, or lies within one pixel of "
"the grid from it, is a *growth alert*, linked to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:505
msgid ""
"A cluster under the minimum size is kept when it touches the earlier "
"alert: it is a growth alert *under the minimum area* (unless **Keep "
"smaller clusters that touch earlier confirmed loss** is cleared). A small"
" cluster that touches nothing is set aside, and the look-back can still "
"bring it back in the next period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:506
msgid ""
"The run looks for earlier alerts in every earlier period, whatever the "
"look-back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:508
msgid ""
"Growth: a confirmed alert grows at its edge in the next period, and the "
"small new cluster is kept and linked to it, while a small cluster that "
"touches nothing is set aside"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:511
msgid ""
"The alerts linked to each other, across all periods, make the *history* "
"of a clearing. Analysis shows it on each alert (see `Earlier alerts "
"<defo-analysis-earlier_>`_), and the `Overview <defo-overview-growth_>`_ "
"sums it up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:515
msgid ""
"Only the reviews saved when `Integrate & vectorize <defo-integrate_>`_ "
"starts count. Review the alerts of a period before you run the next one, "
"so that their growth is linked. An alert reviewed later can still be "
"linked by hand in `Earlier alerts <defo-analysis-earlier_>`_."
msgstr ""

