#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:570
msgid ""
"Under the fields, the dialog previews the search window (\"Search window:"
" start → end\"). Select **Add period**: the period is created and becomes"
" the active period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:572
msgid ""
"A new period starts with the mask choices of the latest period. Change "
"them in `Harmonize <defo-harmonize_>`_. Its alert sources are the ones "
"marked **Add to new periods** in `Alerts <defo-alerts-new-periods_>`_; "
"add or remove sources there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:576
msgid ""
"For the set-aside clusters to come back, the look-back must reach into "
"the previous period. With a look-back of 0, the search window starts on "
"the period's own first day and nothing set aside earlier is reconsidered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:578
msgid ""
"A cluster that stays too small stays in play in later periods for as long"
" as their look-back reaches back to its pixels. A longer look-back gives "
"a slowly growing clearing more time to reach the minimum size, but makes "
"every download bigger (see `What earlier periods already reported <defo-"
"integrate-earlier_>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:581
msgid "Change a period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:583
msgid ""
"For a period without alert sets, the pencil icon opens a dialog to change"
" its dates. New dates give the period a new identity: its downloads and "
"harmonized files are deleted, because they were made for the old window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:585
msgid ""
"A period with alert sets has fixed dates (its note reads **Its dates are "
"fixed: it has alert sets.**). The pencil icon then opens a dialog where "
"only the look-back can change. The period's downloads then show as out of"
" date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:588
msgid "Delete a period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:590
msgid ""
"Select the bin icon. The confirmation dialog lists what is deleted: the "
"period's downloads and harmonized files, and its alert sets with their "
"reviewed alerts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:594
msgid ""
"A period with alert sets can be deleted only when it is the latest "
"period. An earlier period's sets are the footprint the later sets were "
"built from, so delete the later periods first. Periods cannot change or "
"be deleted while a task is writing into the project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:599
msgid "Alert sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:601
msgid ""
"An *alert source* is a dataset of forest-loss alerts. Each alert pixel is"
" *confirmed* (high confidence) or *probable* (low confidence) and carries"
" the day it was first detected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:603
msgid ""
"The **Alerts** step lists the sources of the active `period <defo-"
"period_>`_, shows how much of the AOI and of the period each one covers, "
"and downloads them. Each period has its own sources: a source added here "
"is added to the active period only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:605
msgid ""
"Open the **Alerts** step of the **Workflow** panel. It unlocks once the "
"project has a `period <defo-period_>`_. It works on the active period: to"
" work on another period, make it active in the `Period <defo-period_>`_ "
"step first. The box at the top of the step names the period and its "
"search window, e.g. \"Period 2026-09-01 → 2026-09-30 · search window from"
" 2026-06-03 (90 days of look-back)\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:609
msgid "The Alerts step with three downloaded sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:613
msgid "The source list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:615
msgid "Each row of **Sources** shows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:621
msgid "Part of the row"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:623
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:706
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:968
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1026
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1084
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1427
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2262
msgid "**Source**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:624
msgid ""
"The source's name, then a line with what the row holds (\"downloaded "
"2026-10-20 · 4.7 MB\") or why it needs a download (e.g. \"the search "
"window changed (…): download again\"), and two chips:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:626
msgid ""
"**AOI**: the share of the AOI inside the source's footprint, e.g. \"AOI "
"100 %\". A source that covers only part of the AOI gets no alerts over "
"the rest of it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:627
msgid ""
"The dates: \"✓ data to 2026-10-30\" (green) when the source has data up "
"to the end of the search window, \"data to … only\" (orange) when its "
"data stop inside the window, or \"✗ data ends …\" (red) when it has none "
"in the window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:629
msgid ""
"A points or polygons source has one chip instead, \"clipped to the AOI\":"
" its coverage is not checked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:630
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:998
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1028
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2634
msgid "**Status**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:631
msgid ""
"The row's state, or a button to download it (see `Download the sources "
"<defo-alerts-download_>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:632
msgid "Map icon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:633
msgid ""
"Shows the source on the map: the alerts of the active period's search "
"window. A GeoTIFF source is shown only once it is harmonized. A points or"
" polygons source shows its features as read from the file, once its row "
"is read (see `Points or polygons file <defo-alerts-vector_>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:634
msgid "Information icon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:635
msgid ""
"Opens the source's **Details** (see `The Details dialog <defo-harmonize-"
"details_>`_), with the **Add to new periods** checkbox and, for a custom "
"source, the **Edit** button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:636
msgid "**Download again**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:637
msgid "Downloads the source again (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:638
msgid "**Remove from this period**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:639
msgid ""
"Removes the source from the active period (see `Remove a source from a "
"period <defo-alerts-remove_>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:641
msgid ""
"The coverage is checked once, when the AOI is chosen, and saved in the "
"project. If the check failed (e.g. GEE was not reachable), a **Check "
"again** button appears under the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:644
msgid "Add a source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:646
msgid ""
"Select **Add source** to open the **Add an alert source** dialog, then "
"choose the **Source type**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:648
msgid ""
"**Predefined or project source**: one of the catalogue sources, or a "
"source of the project that is not in this period (e.g. one used in an "
"earlier period); or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:649
msgid ""
"**Custom (0 of 6)**: your own GEE image, image collection or GeoTIFF, or "
"a file of dated points or polygons. The count shows how many of the "
"period's six custom slots are in use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:651
msgid ""
"A period holds at most three predefined and six custom sources. The "
"project keeps every source it has used, with no limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:655
msgid ""
"Under the source, the **Add to new periods** checkbox (selected by "
"default) decides whether the periods created later start with this "
"source. It never changes the existing periods. To change it later, open "
"the source's **Details** with its information icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:658
msgid "Predefined sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:662
msgid "Adding a predefined source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:665
msgid ""
"Choose a source in the **Alert source** dropdown menu, then select **Add "
"source**. The list holds the predefined sources and the project's own "
"sources that are not in this period yet. Each entry shows its coverage of"
" the AOI. A source that does not cover the AOI at all is listed as "
"disabled, with the reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:671
msgid "Source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:672
msgid "Sensor and pixel size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:673
msgid "Coverage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:674
msgid "**GLAD-L (Landsat, 30 m)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:675
msgid "Landsat, about 30 m."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:676
msgid ""
"The land of its four regional tiles (Asia, Africa, Central and South "
"America), between about 35°S and 35°N."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:677
msgid "**RADD (Sentinel-1, 10 m)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:678
msgid "Sentinel-1 radar, 10 m. Sees through clouds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:679
msgid ""
"The humid tropics of Africa, Southeast Asia, and Central and South "
"America. It detects only in primary humid tropical forest; elsewhere in "
"its area, it reports no alerts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:680
msgid "**GLAD-S2 (Sentinel-2, 10 m)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:681
msgid "Sentinel-2, 10 m."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:682
msgid "90°W–30°W, 20°S–20°N."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:684
msgid ""
"When every source is in the period, the dialog reads: \"Every source is "
"already in this period.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:687
msgid "Custom sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:691
msgid "Adding a custom source from an Earth Engine asset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:694
msgid ""
"A custom source reads your own alert raster through one of four format "
"presets. The form reads from top to bottom: the name, where the raster "
"comes from, the raster itself, then its bands. The bands are read as soon"
" as the raster is chosen (\"Reading the bands…\"), and the fields that "
"depend on them appear only once they are read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:703
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:965
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1424
msgid "**Name**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:704
msgid "The source's name in lists, legends and file names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:705
msgid ""
"Suggested from the asset or file name. At most 24 characters, at least "
"one letter or digit, unique in the project. GLAD-L, RADD and GLAD-S2 are "
"reserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:707
msgid ""
"Where the raster is read from: **Earth Engine** (an asset) or **GeoTIFF /"
" VRT** (a file in your SEPAL folder: a GeoTIFF, or a VRT, a GDAL virtual "
"raster read like the GeoTIFFs it points to). The third choice, **Points "
"or polygons file (CSV, GPKG, SHP)**, is not a raster (see `Points or "
"polygons file <defo-alerts-vector_>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:708
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:970
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1429
msgid "**Earth Engine**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:709
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:971
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1430
msgid "Asset or **GeoTIFF / VRT**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:710
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:972
msgid "The GEE image or image collection, or the .tif file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:711
msgid ""
"An image collection is used whole, the newest image on top. For a "
"collection of weekly snapshots (like RADD's own), give the latest image's"
" ID instead. The GeoTIFF needs a coordinate reference system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:712
msgid "**Alert format**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:713
msgid ""
"How the bands are read (see below). Shown when the raster has two bands "
"or more. A raster with one band has no format to choose: the form reads "
"\"One band (…): read as the alert date.\" and the source is read as "
"**Date only**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:714
msgid ""
"Suggested from the band names when the app recognizes them, and marked "
"\"(suggested)\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:715
msgid "**Alert band**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:716
msgid "The band holding the alert class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:717
msgid ""
"Only for **RADD**, **SEPAL CCDC alerts** and **SEPAL PyEO alerts**. "
"Starts on the band the format expects; when the raster has no such band, "
"the hint reads \"Pick the band that holds the alert level.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:718
msgid "**Date band**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:719
msgid "The band holding the detection date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:720
msgid ""
"Always required. Starts on the band the format expects, and its hint "
"names it (e.g. \"3 bands. Date looks like the alert date.\"), or asks you"
" to pick it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:721
msgid "**Date encoding**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:722
msgid ""
"How the date is written: **yymm (year and month; the alert is dated on "
"the 1st)**, **yyddd (year and day of year)**, **yyyyddd (year and day of "
"year)** or **decimal year**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:723
msgid "Only for **Date only**. Suggested from the date band's values (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:725
msgid ""
"For a **Date only** source, the app reads the lowest and highest values "
"of the date band over the AOI (\"Reading the date values…\") and suggests"
" the encoding they fit, for example \"Values from 24001 to 24366: they "
"read as yyddd.\" Check the suggestion: the app reads only the two ends of"
" the range. When the values do not look like dates (\"… don't look like "
"dates. Check the Date band.\"), or when no pixel over the AOI has a date "
"(\"No dated pixel over the AOI: pick the encoding.\"), choose the "
"encoding yourself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:727
msgid "The four formats:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:733
msgid "Alert format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:734
msgid "How a pixel becomes an alert"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:735
msgid "**RADD**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:736
msgid "Alert band: 2 is probable, 3 is confirmed. Date band in ``yyddd``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:737
msgid "**SEPAL CCDC alerts**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:738
msgid ""
"Continuous Change Detection and Classification (CCDC) outputs. "
"``detection_count``: one or two detections are probable, three or more "
"are confirmed. ``first_detection_date`` in fractional years."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:739
msgid "**SEPAL PyEO alerts**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:740
msgid ""
"Outputs of the Python for Earth Observation (PyEO) change detection, read"
" like CCDC. ``total_changes``: one or two changes are probable, three or "
"more are confirmed. ``first_change_date_above_threshold`` in fractional "
"years."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:741
msgid "**Date only**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:742
msgid ""
"One date band in the chosen encoding. Every dated pixel is a confirmed "
"alert."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:744
msgid ""
"When **Add source** is selected, the app checks the raster: the bands "
"exist and are numeric, the dates can be read and the source covers the "
"AOI. A problem is shown in red inside the dialog, which stays open for "
"corrections. While the check runs, the button reads **Cancel** and stops "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:749
msgid "Points or polygons file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:753
msgid "Adding a custom source from a file of points"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:756
msgid ""
"A custom source can also be a file of dated points or polygons, such as "
"alerts reported from the field or by another system. Choose **Points or "
"polygons file (CSV, GPKG, SHP)** in **Source**, then pick the file in "
"**Vector file**: a .csv table, a GeoPackage (.gpkg) or a Shapefile (.shp,"
" with its .shx and .dbf files next to it). The file is read at once "
"(\"Reading the file…\"), and the fields that depend on it appear:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:765
msgid "**Layer**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:766
msgid "The GeoPackage layer to read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:767
msgid "Only for a GeoPackage with several layers. Starts on the first one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:768
msgid "**Longitude column** and **Latitude column**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:769
msgid "The columns holding the coordinates of each point, in degrees (WGS84)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:770
msgid ""
"Only for a CSV. Suggested from the column names (e.g. ``lon``, "
"``latitude``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:771
msgid "**Date column**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:772
msgid "The column holding the date of each alert."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:773
msgid "Suggested from the column names (e.g. ``date``, ``fecha``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:774
msgid "**Dates are written**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:775
msgid "**Day first (dd/mm/yyyy)** or **Month first (mm/dd/yyyy)**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:776
msgid "Only when the dates read either way (e.g. 03/04/2026)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:777
msgid "**Square side (m)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:778
msgid "Each point becomes a square of this side, centred on the point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:779
msgid "Only when the file has points. 30 m by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:781
msgid ""
"A line under the fields sums up what is read, for example \"Dates read as"
" day/month/year · 12 points, 0 polygons · 2026-06-12 → 2026-09-11 · 0 "
"skipped\". Rows without a point or polygon, or without a date, are "
"skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:783
msgid "How the file is read:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:785
msgid ""
"A CSV's columns can be separated by commas, semicolons or tabs. With "
"semicolons, decimal commas are read too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:786
msgid ""
"A GeoPackage or a Shapefile needs a coordinate system, which can be any "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:787
msgid ""
"A date can be a date field, year-month-day (``2026-09-14``), ``yyyymmdd``"
" (``20260914``) or day and month in either order (``14/09/2026``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:788
msgid ""
"Every point or polygon is a confirmed alert. A polygon keeps its shape; a"
" polygon or a square smaller than a pixel still gives one pixel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:789
msgid "Where features overlap, the earliest date is kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:791
msgid ""
"The source needs no GEE: its coverage is not checked, and only the "
"features inside the AOI become alert pixels. Its row in `Alerts <defo-"
"alerts-download_>`_ reads the features of the period's search window "
"(**Read file**); its map icon then shows them as read, points as dots and"
" polygons as outlines. `Harmonize <defo-harmonize_>`_ turns them into "
"alert pixels on the project grid, and its map icon shows that raster, to "
"compare with the features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:793
msgid ""
"**Read file** reads the file again when it was edited after the source "
"was added. If the edit no longer fits the source (for example, a chosen "
"column is gone, or the dates now read in the other day/month order), the "
"row shows \"The alert file changed since it was added. Edit the source to"
" check it again.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:796
msgid "Edit a custom source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:798
msgid ""
"Open the source's **Details** with its information icon, then select "
"**Edit** to reopen the form, titled with the source's name. The name is "
"fixed; the raster, format and bands can change. The form keeps the saved "
"format and bands until another raster is chosen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:800
msgid ""
"Once an alert set uses the source, it can no longer be edited: remove it "
"and add a new one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:805
msgid "Download the sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:807
msgid ""
"Each source is downloaded over the period's search window, in its own "
"projection and cut to the AOI. A GeoTIFF source is not downloaded: it is "
"read from its file. What this guide says of a GeoTIFF source holds for a "
"points or polygons source too; the line under its name reads "
"\"Points/polygons file\". Downloading does not harmonize the source: that"
" is the next step, `Harmonize <defo-harmonize_>`_, which runs only when "
"you start it there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:809
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1031
msgid "The **Status** column reads:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:815
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1037
msgid "Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:816
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1038
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:817
msgid "\"Downloaded\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:818
msgid ""
"Downloaded for the current search window. The line under the name gives "
"the download date and the size on disk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:819
msgid "**Download**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:820
msgid ""
"The source is not downloaded for this period's search window yet, or its "
"download is out of date. Select the button to download it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:821
msgid "**Read file**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:822
msgid "The same for a GeoTIFF source, which is read from its file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:823
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1045
msgid "**Retry**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:824
msgid "The last download failed. Its error is shown in red under the row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:825
msgid "\"Downloading 42%\", \"Reading\", \"Queued\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:826
msgid "The row is running, or waits for its turn (\"waiting for the row above\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:827
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1049
msgid "\"not covered\", \"no data\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:828
msgid ""
"The source cannot run for this period: it does not cover the AOI, or it "
"has no data for the search window (its dates chip is red)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:829
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1051
msgid "\"File missing\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:830
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1052
msgid ""
"The file of a GeoTIFF source is gone (see `Common messages <defo-"
"harmonize-messages_>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:832
msgid ""
"A blue button runs a row for the first time; an orange one redoes a file "
"that is out of date. The line under the name then says why: for example "
"\"the search window changed (…): download again\" or \"the AOI changed: "
"download again\". In an evaluator's `review copy <defo-evaluation-"
"return_>`_, nothing runs: the column reads \"To download\" instead of a "
"button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:836
msgid ""
"A downloaded row has no button: a source already downloaded for the "
"period's search window is not downloaded again by itself. To fetch the "
"latest alerts of a catalogue that keeps adding alerts to past dates, use "
"**Download again**. The app asks first, with the window and the date of "
"the file it replaces. It is not offered for a GeoTIFF source (\"Nothing "
"to download again: read from a file\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:838
msgid ""
"Each row is downloaded with its own button. Select the buttons of several"
" rows to download them all: each starts its own job, and they queue, one "
"row at a time. Rows that read \"not covered\" or \"no data\" have no "
"button; a row that fails shows its error in red under it. The running row"
" shows its own progress bar; a started row cannot be stopped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:840
msgid ""
"The download also shows as a task notification titled **Download**, with "
"the source it is on and its percentage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:845
msgid "Remove a source from a period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:847
msgid ""
"Select the bin icon (**Remove from this period**), then confirm. The "
"source's downloaded and harmonized files of this period are deleted. "
"Alert sets of this period that already used it keep their alerts and show"
" as out of date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:849
msgid ""
"The source stays in the project: other periods keep it, and it can be "
"added back with **Add source**. A source is never deleted from the whole "
"project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:852
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1115
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1351
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1535
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1987
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2511
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2712
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2851
msgid "Common messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:854
msgid "\"This source does not cover the AOI.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:855
msgid "The raster's footprint misses the area: check the asset or the AOI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:857
msgid "\"A mapped band is missing.\" or \"A mapped band is not numeric.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:858
msgid "Choose other bands or another format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:860
msgid "\"This CCDC asset stores its dates as Julian days or Unix time …\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:861
msgid "Only CCDC outputs dated in fractional years are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:863
msgid "\"This period already has 6 custom sources.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:864
msgid "Remove a custom source from the period before adding another one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:866
msgid "\"This file cannot be read as CSV, GeoPackage or Shapefile.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:867
msgid ""
"The file is not a .csv, .gpkg or .shp file, or it could not be read as "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:869
msgid "\"The Shapefile is missing its .shx or .dbf file.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:870
msgid "Put the .shx and .dbf files with the same name as the .shp in its folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:872
msgid ""
"\"The date column cannot be read: mixed day/month orders or no valid "
"date.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:873
msgid ""
"Some dates are written day first and others month first, or no value "
"reads as a date. Choose another **Date column**, or write the dates in "
"one format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:875
msgid "\"No dated point or polygon in this file.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:876
msgid ""
"No row has both a point or polygon and a date. Line features and rows "
"without coordinates are skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:878
msgid "\"A job is writing into this project; …\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:879
msgid ""
"Sources cannot change during a download or an **Integrate & vectorize** "
"run. Wait for it to end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:884
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2924
msgid "Harmonize"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:886
msgid ""
"This step puts every input of the active `period <defo-period_>`_ on one "
"common grid. Each source downloaded in `Alerts <defo-alerts-download_>`_ "
"is *harmonized*: aligned onto the project grid and cut by the period's "
"masks. Nothing whose inputs are unchanged runs twice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:888
msgid ""
"Open the **Harmonize** step of the **Workflow** panel. It unlocks once at"
" least one source of the active period is downloaded (or is a GeoTIFF "
"source). It works on the active period: to harmonize another period, make"
" it active in the `Period <defo-period_>`_ step first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:890
msgid ""
"From top to bottom, the step has three parts: the **Project grid**, the "
"**Masks** and the **Sources for this period**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:894
msgid "The Harmonize step after a run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:898
msgid "The project grid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:900
msgid ""
"Every raster of the project is aligned onto one grid: one projection in "
"metres and one pixel size, over the AOI. Alerts from sources with "
"different pixel sizes can then be combined pixel by pixel, and the "
"minimum alert size in hectares becomes a pixel count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:909
msgid "**EPSG**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:910
msgid ""
"The projection of the grid, as a European Petroleum Survey Group (EPSG) "
"code. The target button at the end of the field fills in the Universal "
"Transverse Mercator (UTM) zone of the AOI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:911
msgid ""
"The UTM zone of the AOI's centre. Must be a projected system in metres: a"
" geographic system (like 4326) or one in feet is refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:912
msgid "**Resolution**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:913
msgid "The pixel size, in metres."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:914
msgid ""
"The finest pixel size among the project's sources: 10 m with RADD or "
"GLAD-S2, 30 m with GLAD-L only, a custom source's own pixel size, or 30 m"
" when nothing is known. Must be greater than 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:916
msgid ""
"Under the fields, the grid's size is previewed: \"width × height pixels, "
"about … per source before compression\". Above 2 GB per source, a warning"
" reads **This grid is large: downloads will take a while and use disk "
"space.** (it does not block the step)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:918
msgid ""
"Select **Save grid**. The masks and the sources table appear only once a "
"grid is saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:920
msgid ""
"The grid can change until the first alert set is made. A new grid only "
"harmonizes the sources again from the files already downloaded; it does "
"not download them again. Once the project has an alert set, the card "
"reads **The grid is locked because the project has alert sets.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:924
msgid ""
"Changing the `AOI <defo-aoi_>`_ clears the grid and deletes every "
"download and harmonized file of the project, which were made for the old "
"area. Save the grid again here, then run the rows again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:927
msgid "Masks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:929
msgid ""
"A *mask* limits where alerts are kept. It is a raster defined once for "
"the project: a GEE image or image collection, or a GeoTIFF, with one "
"band. A pixel is inside the mask where that band is not zero; zero and "
"no-data pixels are outside it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:931
msgid "Each period chooses a **Mode** for each mask:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:937
msgid "Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:938
msgid "Effect on the period's alerts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:939
msgid "**Off**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:940
msgid "The mask is not used in this period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:941
msgid "**Keep**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:942
msgid ""
"Alerts *outside* the mask are removed (e.g. keep only alerts inside a "
"forest mask)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:943
msgid "**Exclude**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:944
msgid ""
"Alerts *inside* the mask are removed (e.g. drop alerts in plantations or "
"water)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:946
msgid ""
"When several masks are on, all of them apply. Masks act on the harmonized"
" sources, so a change of **Mode** makes the period's sources out of date."
" The **Harmonize** of each row then harmonizes them again without "
"downloading them. A new period starts with the mask choices of the latest"
" period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:949
msgid "Add a mask"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:953
msgid "Adding a mask"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:956
msgid ""
"Select **Add mask** to open the **Add a mask** dialog. The bands are read"
" as soon as the raster is chosen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:966
msgid "The mask's name in lists, legends and file names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:967
msgid ""
"Suggested from the asset or file name. At most 24 characters, at least "
"one letter or digit, unique among the project's masks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:969
msgid ""
"**Earth Engine** (an asset) or **GeoTIFF / VRT** (a file in your SEPAL "
"folder)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:974
msgid "**Band**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:975
msgid ""
"The band that defines the mask. Shown when the raster has two bands or "
"more; with one band, the form reads \"One band (…): the mask is made from"
" it.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:976
msgid ""
"The band whose name looks like a mask (e.g. ``datamask``), named in the "
"hint (\"… looks like a mask; non-zero pixels are inside it.\"), else "
"none: pick it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:977
msgid "**Mode in the active period**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:978
msgid "**Keep** or **Exclude**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:979
msgid ""
"**Keep**. The mask is turned on in the active period only; every other "
"period leaves it off until it is turned on there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:981
msgid ""
"When **Add mask** is selected, the app checks the raster and its band. A "
"problem is shown in red inside the dialog, which stays open for "
"corrections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:984
msgid "The mask list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:986
msgid "Each row of **Masks** shows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:994
msgid "**Mask**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:995
msgid ""
"The mask's name. The line under it gives its source and size on disk once"
" it is ready (\"Earth Engine · 18.9 MB\"), or why it needs a run (\"not "
"downloaded yet\", \"the grid changed (…): align again\"). It ends with "
"\"Off\" when the mask is off in the active period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:996
msgid "**Mode**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:997
msgid ""
"The mask's mode in the active period: **Off**, **Keep** or **Exclude**. A"
" change applies at once; the period's sources then read out of date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:999
msgid ""
"\"Ready\", or a button for the mask's next run: **Download** (a GEE mask "
"not downloaded yet) or **Align** (onto the grid). An orange button redoes"
" a file that is out of date. While a run goes on, the cell reads "
"\"Downloading 42%\", \"Aligning\" or \"Queued\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1003
msgid ""
"the map icon shows the mask on the map: a GEE mask can be previewed "
"before it is downloaded, a GeoTIFF mask once it is aligned;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1004
msgid ""
"the information icon opens its **Details** (see `The Details dialog "
"<defo-harmonize-details_>`_); and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1005
msgid "the **More actions** menu (three dots) holds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1007
msgid ""
"**Download again** (GEE masks only), for an asset that changed. The app "
"asks first: \"This fetches the mask again from Earth Engine, replaces its"
" download, then aligns it.\";"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1008
msgid ""
"**Edit**, which opens **Edit mask** *name*: the raster and band can "
"change, the name cannot. Once an alert set used the mask, it can no "
"longer be edited (**An alert set already uses this mask: add a new one "
"instead.**); and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1009
msgid ""
"**Delete mask…**, which deletes the mask after you confirm. Its download "
"and aligned file are deleted and every period stops using it. Alert sets "
"that used it keep their alerts and show as out of date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1011
msgid ""
"A mask is downloaded and aligned once for the whole project, whichever "
"period runs it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1016
msgid "Sources for this period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1018
msgid ""
"The table has one row per alert source of the active period, with two "
"columns:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1027
msgid ""
"The source's name. The line under it says what the row holds or what it "
"waits for (see below). Warnings, such as a partial coverage, and errors "
"show as lines under the row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1029
msgid "The row's state, or a button for its next run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1039
msgid "\"Ready\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1040
msgid ""
"Downloaded and harmonized with the current inputs. The line under the "
"name gives the download date, the size on disk and what the harmonized "
"file found: \"downloaded 2026-10-20 · 31.7 MB · 2,362,718 alert pixels\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1041
msgid "**Harmonize**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1042
msgid ""
"The download is current, but the harmonized file is missing or out of "
"date (a new download, a new grid, a mask change). Select the button to "
"run the row: it aligns any mask of the period that needs it, then "
"harmonizes the source, without downloading it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1043
msgid "\"Download or read it in Alerts first\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1044
msgid ""
"The source is not downloaded for this period's search window, or its "
"download is out of date. The row has no button: download it in `Alerts "
"<defo-alerts-download_>`_ first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1046
msgid "The last run of the row failed. Its error is shown in red under the row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1047
msgid "\"Downloading 42%\", \"Harmonizing\", \"Queued\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1048
msgid ""
"The row is running, or waits for its turn in a run (\"waiting for the row"
" above\"). A row being downloaded in Alerts shows as running here too, "
"and cannot be harmonized until its download ends."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1050
msgid ""
"The source cannot run for this period: it does not cover the AOI, or it "
"has no data for the search window. The line under the name gives the "
"reason. See `Alert sources <defo-alerts_>`_ for coverage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1054
msgid ""
"In an evaluator's `review copy <defo-evaluation-return_>`_, nothing runs:"
" instead of a button, the column reads \"To harmonize\" or \"To align\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1056
msgid ""
"A blue button runs a row for the first time; an orange one redoes a file "
"that is out of date. The line under the name then says why: for example "
"\"the grid changed (EPSG:32719 · 30 m → EPSG:32719 · 10 m): harmonize "
"again\", \"it was downloaded again since: harmonize again\" or \"mask "
"forest_2000 changed: harmonize again\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1060
msgid "the map icon (**Show on the map**) shows the harmonized alerts on the map;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1061
msgid "the information icon opens the row's **Details** (see below); and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1062
msgid ""
"**Delete harmonized file** removes this period's harmonized file of the "
"source, after you confirm. The download stays: harmonize the source again"
" in this step to rebuild the file. The alert sets of this period built "
"from the source read out of date; their alerts and reviews stay."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1067
msgid "The Details dialog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1071
msgid "The Details dialog of a source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1074
msgid ""
"The information icon of a source or a mask opens a read-only summary of "
"what its files were made with. It starts with the row's status and, for a"
" source, the period. When the row is out of date, an orange **Why:** line"
" says what changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1076
msgid ""
"In `Alerts <defo-alerts_>`_, the information icon of a source opens the "
"same dialog, with two more controls: the **Add to new periods** checkbox "
"(see `Add a source <defo-alerts-new-periods_>`_) and, for a custom "
"source, **Edit**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1082
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2162
msgid "Section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1083
msgid "What it lists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1085
msgid ""
"A predefined source: its **Catalogue** and **Coverage** of the AOI, with "
"the last date of data and the day it was checked. A custom source: its "
"**Kind**, **Reference**, **Format**, **Date encoding**, **Bands** and "
"**Native grid**. A points or polygons source: its **Kind**, "
"**Reference**, **Layer**, **Date column** (with how its dates are read) "
"and **Square side (m)**. A mask: its **Reference**, **Band**, **Native "
"grid** and the periods it is **Used in**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1086
msgid "**Download** (**Read from file** for a GeoTIFF source)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1087
msgid ""
"The **Search window**, the **Native grid** the file was downloaded in, "
"its **Size** and its **File** in the project folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1088
msgid "**Harmonize** (**Align** for a mask)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1089
msgid ""
"The **Grid used**, with the current grid when it changed since, the "
"**Resampling**, the **Masks** applied with their mode, the **Alert "
"pixels** kept (and how many the masks removed), the **Alert dates** "
"found, the **Size** and the **File**. For a mask: its **Mask pixels**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1091
msgid ""
"Each section gives the date and time its file was written, or reads \"Not"
" run yet\". Select **Close**, or press **Esc**, to close the dialog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1096
msgid "Run several rows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1098
msgid ""
"Each row runs with its own button. A source's **Harmonize** first aligns "
"the masks on in the period that need it, then harmonizes the source; a "
"mask's **Align** aligns only that mask. Select the buttons of several "
"rows to run them all: each starts its own job, and they queue, one row at"
" a time:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1100
msgid ""
"rows that read \"not covered\" or \"no data\", and rows still to "
"download, have no button;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1101
msgid ""
"a row that fails shows its error in red under it, and the next row goes "
"on;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1102
msgid ""
"while one source's run aligns a mask, another source's **Harmonize** that"
" needs the same mask reads \"Queued\" and starts once the mask is "
"aligned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1104
msgid ""
"The running row shows its own progress bar, which moves without an end "
"while it has no percentage. A started row cannot be stopped; the rows "
"already done stay done."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1106
msgid ""
"The run also shows as a task notification titled **Harmonize**, with the "
"row it is on (e.g. \"Harmonizing GLAD-L\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1110
msgid ""
"Each row needs free disk space for its files. The app checks it before "
"writing, and stops the row with a message when the disk is too full. The "
"grid size line gives an idea of how big a source can get."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1117
msgid "\"Not enough free disk space: this needs … GB in …, and … GB is free.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1118
msgid "Free some space in your SEPAL folder, or use a coarser grid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1120
msgid "\"A row of this run is already being prepared …\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1121
msgid ""
"The mask whose **Align** you selected is being aligned by another run "
"(another period's, or a source's **Harmonize**), or the row is still "
"running. Run it again once that has finished."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1123
msgid ""
"\"The AOI's geometry is still being fetched; run this row again in a "
"moment.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1124
msgid ""
"GeoTIFF sources and masks need the AOI's shape. Wait a moment. If it "
"could not be fetched, select **Check again** under the table, then run "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1126
msgid ""
"\"Mask … covers none of the AOI: as a keep mask, every alert would be "
"removed.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1127
msgid "The mask misses the area. Check its asset or band, or turn it off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1129
msgid ""
"\"A job is writing into this project; save the grid once it has "
"finished.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1130
msgid ""
"The grid, masks and sources cannot change while a download or an "
"**Integrate & vectorize** run is going."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1132
msgid ""
"\"File missing\", with \"missing: file not found: …\" under the row, or "
"\"Mask …: file not found (…). Put the file back at this path to use the "
"mask.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1133
msgid ""
"A GeoTIFF source or mask was moved, renamed or deleted from your SEPAL "
"folder. Put the file back at the path shown, or edit the source or mask "
"to point at its new place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1135
msgid ""
"\"A mask on in this period is not aligned on the current grid yet; a "
"source's Harmonize aligns the masks first.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1136
msgid ""
"A source cannot be harmonized before the period's masks are aligned. "
"Select the source's **Harmonize**, or the mask's **Align** button first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1138
msgid ""
"\"Mask …: its native grid (projection and scale) is unknown; edit the "
"mask.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1139
msgid ""
"The app does not know how to download this GEE mask. Open it with "
"**Edit** in its **More actions** menu and save it again, so that its "
"raster is checked anew."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1144
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2935
msgid "Integrate & vectorize"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1146
msgid ""
"This step turns the harmonized sources of the active period into an "
"*alert set*: the list of alerts to review in `Analysis <defo-"
"analysis_>`_. It:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1148
msgid "combines the sources pixel by pixel;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1149
msgid "removes what earlier periods already reported;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1150
msgid "groups neighbouring alert pixels into *clusters*; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1151
msgid ""
"draws one polygon per cluster. Each cluster it keeps is an alert of the "
"set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1153
msgid ""
"Open the **Integrate & vectorize** step of the **Workflow** panel. It "
"unlocks once at least one source of the active period is ready in "
"`Harmonize <defo-harmonize_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1155
msgid ""
"The form follows the run, in three outlined cards: the sources to "
"combine, the cluster settings and the attribute layers. The **Integrate &"
" vectorize** button is under them. Under the sources, grey lines say what"
" the run also does on its own, without a setting:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1157
msgid ""
"\"Removes the pixels already in N earlier alert sets\" (see `What earlier"
" periods already reported <defo-integrate-earlier_>`_); and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1158
msgid ""
"\"Brings back the not-analysable pixels of N earlier sets inside the "
"look-back\", counted for the selected sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1162
msgid "The Integrate & vectorize form"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1166
msgid "What an alert is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1168
msgid ""
"An alert is a *cluster*: a group of alert pixels that touch each other, "
"by their sides or corners, whichever source flagged each pixel. Where "
"GLAD-L and RADD pixels touch, they form *one* alert that lists both "
"sources. An alert is never split into one alert per source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1170
msgid "Each alert keeps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1172
msgid "the sources that detected it;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1173
msgid ""
"its first and last detection dates (the earliest and latest date among "
"its pixels);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1174
msgid "its area in hectares; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1175
msgid "a statistic of each attribute layer's bands (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1177
msgid ""
"A cluster smaller than the **Minimum cluster size** (see `The options "
"<defo-integrate-options_>`_) does not become an alert: its pixels are set"
" aside as *not analysable*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1179
msgid ""
"Sources on one grid become clusters; each cluster is measured against the"
" minimum size, and becomes one polygon listing its sources or, when "
"smaller, is set aside"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1185
msgid "What earlier periods already reported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1187
msgid ""
"Pixels inside the alerts of an alert set from an *earlier* period (its "
"*footprint*) are removed before the clusters are made. This way, the "
"`look-back <defo-period-lookback_>`_ never reports the same loss twice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1189
msgid ""
"Pixels that did not become alerts (a cluster below the minimum size, or "
"beyond the maximum number of alerts) are kept as *not analysable*. They "
"are not in the footprint: bringing them back is the purpose of the `look-"
"back <defo-period-lookback_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1191
msgid "A later period's run adds those pixels back when both conditions are met:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1193
msgid ""
"its look-back reaches back into the earlier period (that period ends on "
"or after the start of the new search window); and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1194
msgid "the two periods share a source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1196
msgid ""
"The pixels come back whatever their detection date within the earlier "
"set's own search window. They join the new pixels that touch them, and a "
"cluster that now reaches the minimum size becomes an alert. Its detection"
" dates can be older than its own period and look-back. With a look-back "
"of 0, the search window starts on the period's own first day, so nothing "
"set aside is reconsidered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1201
msgid "Growth of earlier loss"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1203
msgid ""
"A clearing often keeps growing from one month to the next. The run links "
"each new alert to the *earlier loss* it grows from: the alerts of earlier"
" periods' sets that were saved as **True alert** or **Needs revision**. "
"An earlier alert's shape is the polygon drawn for it in `Refine the "
"polygon <defo-analysis-refine_>`_, or else its detected cluster."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1205
msgid ""
"A new cluster that lies within one pixel of the grid of an earlier "
"alert's shape, edge to edge, is a *growth alert*, linked to every earlier"
" alert that close. A cluster one empty pixel away still counts; a "
"diagonal gap of one pixel is farther. One without a link is a *new* "
"alert."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1206
msgid ""
"With **Keep smaller clusters that touch earlier confirmed loss** selected"
" (the default), a cluster smaller than the **Minimum cluster size** is "
"kept when it is that close to earlier loss: it is a growth alert *under "
"the minimum area*. Cleared, every small cluster is set aside. A small "
"cluster that touches nothing is always set aside as *not analysable*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1207
msgid ""
"Growth alerts are sorted and limited with the others: **Limit the number "
"of clusters** can leave them out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1208
msgid ""
"Sets made before this reach of one pixel keep the links they were made "
"with until they are run again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1209
msgid ""
"Only the reviews saved when the run starts count. An earlier alert "
"confirmed afterwards is not linked, but it can be linked by hand in "
"`Earlier alerts <defo-analysis-earlier_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1211
msgid ""
"The alerts linked to each other, across all periods, make the *history* "
"of a clearing. Analysis shows it on each alert, and the `Overview <defo-"
"overview-growth_>`_ sums it up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1216
msgid "The options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1218
msgid ""
"The form opens with the settings of the active alert set (all but the "
"sources), or with the defaults below when there is none."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1224
msgid "Option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1227
msgid "Sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1228
msgid ""
"The sources whose alerts go into the set, in the first card. Each ready "
"source is listed with what its harmonized file found. A source that does "
"not cover the AOI, or has no data for the period, is listed as disabled, "
"with the reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1229
msgid "Every ready source. At least one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1230
msgid "**Include probable (unconfirmed) alerts**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1231
msgid ""
"Shown only when at least one selected source has a *probable* (low-"
"confidence) class. One switch for all such sources. Off, their probable "
"pixels are dropped before anything else, and only their confirmed pixels "
"count. With two or more such sources, **Set per source** unfolds one "
"switch per source (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1232
msgid "On."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1233
msgid "**Minimum cluster size**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1234
msgid ""
"Clusters smaller than this are dropped, unless the next option keeps "
"them. The hint gives that size in pixels of the grid (at 10 m, 0.5 ha is "
"\"50 pixels on the grid\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1235
msgid ""
"0.5 ha. Any number of hectares, 0 or more. Even at 0, a cluster is at "
"least one pixel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1236
msgid "**Keep smaller clusters that touch earlier confirmed loss**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1237
msgid ""
"Keeps a cluster under the minimum size when it is within one pixel of an "
"earlier alert reviewed as **True alert** or **Needs revision** (see "
"`Growth of earlier loss <defo-integrate-growth_>`_). A line under it says"
" when the run has nothing to link to: \"No earlier period has an alert "
"set yet: nothing links in this run.\" or \"No alert of an earlier period "
"is reviewed yet: nothing links in this run.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1238
msgid "Selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1239
msgid "**Order**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1240
msgid ""
"The order of the clusters in the set, which is the review order: **Bigger"
" clusters first**, **Smaller clusters first**, **Recent clusters first** "
"(by last detection date) or **Older clusters first** (by first detection "
"date)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1241
msgid "**Bigger clusters first**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1242
msgid "**Limit the number of clusters**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1243
msgid ""
"When selected, shows **Maximum number of clusters**: only the first "
"clusters in the chosen **Order** are kept. Its hint says which (e.g. "
"\"Keeps the 100 biggest clusters.\" or \"Keeps the 100 most recent "
"clusters.\"). When cleared, every cluster is kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1244
msgid ""
"Cleared. When selected, the limit starts at 100. It must be a whole "
"number greater than 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1245
msgid "**Attribute layers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1246
msgid "Rasters whose band statistics are added to every alert (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1247
msgid "None."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1250
msgid "Probable alerts per source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1252
msgid ""
"With two or more selected sources that have a probable class, select "
"**Set per source** under **Include probable (unconfirmed) alerts** to "
"give each one its own switch, named after the source:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1254
msgid ""
"A selected source without a probable class (a custom source that has only"
" detection dates) is listed as \"(source): dates only, no probable "
"level\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1255
msgid ""
"When the sources' switches differ, the main switch reads off, the note "
"**Mixed: the sources below differ.** replaces **Set per source**, and the"
" per-source switches stay open."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1256
msgid "Turning the main switch on or off sets every source at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1261
msgid "Attribute layers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1263
msgid ""
"An *attribute layer* adds information to each alert from a raster (e.g. "
"the majority land-cover class under the alert, or its mean elevation). "
"The values are columns of the alert table: they are exported with the "
"alerts, and columns of classes can be used in the Analysis filter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1267
msgid "Adding an attribute layer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1270
msgid "To add an attribute layer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1272
msgid ""
"Select **Add attribute layer** to open the **Add an attribute layer** "
"dialog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1273
msgid ""
"Check the **Layer name**, suggested from the raster once it is chosen. "
"The columns are named *layer name*\\_\\ *band*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1274
msgid ""
"Choose the **Source** (**Earth Engine**, an image, or **GeoTIFF / VRT**, "
"a file in your SEPAL folder), then choose the raster. Its bands are read "
"at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1275
msgid ""
"With one band, the form reads \"One band (…): its statistic is added to "
"every cluster.\" With two or more, select one or more in **Bands**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1276
msgid ""
"For each band, choose the statistic computed over the alert: **Majority**"
" (for classes), **Mean**, **Minimum**, **Maximum** or **Median**. It "
"starts on **Majority** when the band's name looks like classes (e.g. "
"``landcover``), and on **Mean** otherwise, marked \"(suggested)\". The "
"column name is shown beside it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1277
msgid "Select **Add attribute layer**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1279
msgid "Rules:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1281
msgid "A layer needs at least one band (**Keep at least one band.**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1282
msgid ""
"Two layers cannot read the same raster (**Another attribute layer already"
" reads this raster.**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1283
msgid ""
"Column names never take the name of an alert column or of another layer's"
" column: a clash gets a suffix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1285
msgid ""
"The list under **Attribute layers** shows each layer with its columns. "
"The pencil icon edits a layer and the bin icon removes it. The layers "
"belong to this form until it runs: they are saved with the alert set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1288
msgid "Run the step"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1290
msgid ""
"The grey line above the button names the set the run makes: \"Creates or "
"replaces the alert set (period) · (sources)\". An alert set is identified"
" by its period and its sources:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1292
msgid ""
"a new combination of sources makes a new set: a period can hold several "
"sets (e.g. one with GLAD-L only and one with all three sources); and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1293
msgid "the same combination again *replaces* the set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1295
msgid ""
"Select **Integrate & vectorize**. The button stays disabled until at "
"least one source is selected and, when **Limit the number of clusters** "
"is selected, the limit is valid (\"Enter a whole number greater than 0.\""
" under the field)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1297
msgid ""
"The run goes through \"Combining sources\", \"Vectorizing clusters\", "
"\"Saving the clusters\", \"Writing the footprint\" and \"Building map "
"tiles\". When it ends, a message reads \"N clusters ready for review\", "
"followed by \"Linked N clusters to earlier loss (M under the minimum "
"area)\" when it found `growth alerts <defo-integrate-growth_>`_, and the "
"new set becomes the *active set*: the one the `Questionnaire <defo-"
"questionnaire_>`_, `Evaluation <defo-evaluation_>`_, `Analysis <defo-"
"analysis_>`_ and `Overview <defo-overview_>`_ work on. The step stays "
"open."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1299
msgid ""
"The run also gives every alert the names of the administrative areas it "
"touches: ``admin1`` is the country, ``admin2`` the first-level unit and "
"``admin3`` the second-level unit, from the FAO GAUL 2024 boundaries. The "
"boundaries are downloaded once for the project's AOI and kept in the "
"project folder (``admin/``). An alert across a border lists every area it"
" touches, separated by commas, the one holding most of it first. If the "
"download fails, the run still ends, with a warning, and the names are "
"filled when an alert is saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1301
msgid ""
"If no cluster is left, the set is still made, empty: the message reads "
"\"No new clusters in this period: the alert set is empty.\" and gives the"
" reason for each source (e.g. \"GLAD-L: all 56 alert pixels removed by "
"masks\" or \"RADD: probable (unconfirmed) alerts were left out\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1306
msgid "Replace a set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1310
msgid "Confirming the replacement of an alert set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1313
msgid ""
"When the set about to be replaced has reviewed alerts or an `evaluator "
"split <defo-evaluation_>`_, the **Replace this alert set?** dialog lists "
"what would be lost: the reviewed alerts (up to 20, then \"… and N "
"more\"), and the split with the reviews that evaluators have not sent "
"back yet. When alerts of later periods grow from this set, it adds \"N "
"clusters of later periods are linked to this set; their links will "
"break.\": after the run, those links show as \"earlier set was re-run\" "
"(see `Earlier alerts <defo-analysis-earlier_>`_). Select **Replace** to "
"continue. A set with nothing to lose is replaced without confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1317
msgid ""
"Replacing a set discards its reviews. To try other settings without "
"losing reviews, choose another combination of sources, which makes a "
"separate set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1322
msgid "When the active set is out of date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1324
msgid ""
"If the inputs of the active set changed since it was made (a source "
"downloaded again, a mask switched, the period's look-back, the AOI or the"
" grid changed), an orange line reads: \"The active set (…) was built from"
" inputs that have changed since.\" Run **Integrate & vectorize** again to"
" rebuild it, which discards its reviews."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1326
msgid ""
"If the set's files were deleted from the project folder, the line reads: "
"\"The active set's files (…) are missing from the project folder.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1331
msgid "View the alerts on the map"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1333
msgid ""
"Once the project has a set, a heading under the button counts the active "
"set's alerts (\"Result · 48 clusters\"), and switches under it draw the "
"set on the map:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1339
msgid "Switch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1341
msgid "**Show these alerts on the map**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1342
msgid ""
"The active set's alerts, coloured by review status. Click on an alert to "
"view \"Alert (id) · (status) · (area) ha\". Its **Review** button opens "
"it in Analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1343
msgid "**Show not-analysable pixels**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1344
msgid ""
"The alert pixels that did not become alerts: **Too small** or **Over the "
"alert cap**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1345
msgid "**Show earlier sets**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1346
msgid "The alerts of earlier periods' sets, for context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1348
msgid "The map keeps them in other steps. Turn them off here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1353
msgid ""
"\"… is not downloaded and harmonized for this period; download it in "
"Alerts and harmonize it in Harmonize first.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1354
msgid ""
"A source's files are out of date. Download it in `Alerts <defo-alerts-"
"download_>`_, then harmonize it in `Harmonize <defo-harmonize_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1356
msgid ""
"\"The footprint of the earlier set … is missing; run Integrate & "
"vectorize on that set again first.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1357
msgid ""
"An earlier period's files were deleted. Make that period active and run "
"its set again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1359
msgid "\"Not enough free disk space: …\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1360
msgid "The run writes a few rasters the size of the grid. Free some space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1362
msgid ""
"\"The project's period, area of interest or grid changed while the run "
"was going, so the alert set was not recorded.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1363
msgid "Run it again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1365
msgid ""
"\"tippecanoe is not installed: the map will show alert points without "
"polygons.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1366
msgid "The set is made; the map shows its alerts as points instead of polygons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1368
msgid ""
"\"The map tiles could not be shown (…): showing alert points without "
"polygons.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1369
msgid ""
"The set is made, but its map layer could not be built. The map shows its "
"alerts as points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:1371
msgid ""
