#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2166
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2692
msgid "**Alerts**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2167
msgid ""
"*Original alert*: the outline of the alert's polygon from `Integrate & "
"vectorize <defo-integrate_>`_, and of the other alerts of its group (see "
"`Nearby alerts <defo-analysis-nearby_>`_), on by default and hidden while"
" drawing. *All alerts*: the alert pixels of the whole set, half "
"transparent (off). *Alert BB*: the alert's bounding box. *Defo Layer*: "
"the polygon saved for the alert (see `Refine the polygon <defo-analysis-"
"refine_>`_). *Earlier alerts* (see `Earlier alerts <defo-analysis-"
"earlier_>`_). *Nearby alerts*, only when nearby alerts are reviewed "
"together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2168
msgid "**Additional layers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2169
msgid ""
"The `additional layers <defo-layers_>`_ marked **Show in Analysis**, "
"turned off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2171
msgid ""
"A map displays \"Imagery failed to load\" when the tiles of its image do "
"not load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2176
msgid "Choose the images: the timeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2180
msgid "The image timeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2183
msgid ""
"The timeline shows every image that covers the alert, from about two "
"months before the alert was first detected to two months after it was "
"last detected. Each image source that is switched on in the **Image "
"sources** menu (see below) has its own band:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2185
msgid "*Sentinel-2* stripes on top;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2186
msgid "*Landsat* in the middle;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2187
msgid ""
"*Planet* (the NICFI monthly mosaic) as a bar across its month, only when "
"your GEE account has NICFI access and you switched it on; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2188
msgid ""
"*Sentinel-1* radar, only when you switched it on, with one band per pass "
"(*Sentinel-1 asc* and *Sentinel-1 desc*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2190
msgid ""
"A faded, half-height stripe is an image over the cloud limit. The gold "
"band is the *alert window*: the dates over which the alert was detected. "
"On a `growth alert <defo-integrate-growth_>`_, a grey band behind it "
"marks the detection dates of each earlier alert it is linked to: choose a"
" before image taken after the earlier clearing to see only the new loss."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2192
msgid ""
"Two handles above the track choose the images: the left one the before "
"image, the right one the after image. The bracket between them states how"
" many days apart they are (\"49 days apart\"), or warns \"the same image "
"on both sides\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2194
msgid "To move a handle, use one of these methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2196
msgid ""
"Drag a handle and release it on the chosen image. The before handle "
"cannot pass the after handle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2197
msgid ""
"Click on a stripe: the nearest suitable handle moves to it. Images over "
"the cloud limit cannot be selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2198
msgid ""
"With the keyboard: press **Tab** to reach a handle, move along the dates "
"with the left and right arrow keys, jump to the first or last image with "
"**Home** and **End**, and choose with **Enter**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2200
msgid ""
"When an alert opens, the app chooses the image nearest *before* the alert"
" window and the image nearest *after* it, among the images under the "
"cloud limit. It never chooses an image inside the alert window (it would "
"show only part of the clearing) or a Planet mosaic, but both can be "
"chosen by hand. A side with no image under the cloud limit gets the least"
" cloudy image within 30 days of the alert window, or the nearest one if "
"there is none, even over the cloud limit (its map title shows its cloud "
"cover); a side with no image at all is left \"not set\". A reviewed alert"
" opens on the images it was saved with. If one of them is no longer "
"available, its map title reads \"Saved image not available; picked "
"automatically\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2202
msgid ""
"Each map's title names its image in an **Optical** chip: \"Before image ·"
" Optical · Sentinel-2 2026-07-28 · 3%\" (collection, date, cloud cover). "
"When the other collection has an image of the same day, a button in the "
"title (\"⇄ Landsat\") switches to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2204
msgid ""
"When Sentinel-1 is on, a thin strip under the optical lane holds its "
"images as dots, with two diamond-shaped handles. The arrow at the left of"
" the strip unfolds it into a lane with one band per pass, and folds it "
"again. The radar handles are hollow while they follow the optical picks: "
"each sits on the radar image nearest to the date of its optical handle "
"(from the same pass as the other radar handle when one is within 30 days,"
" otherwise from either pass) and moves with it. Hollow handles are not "
"saved: they are placed again when the alert opens. Drag one, or click a "
"radar stripe in the unfolded lane, and it becomes filled: it is yours and"
" stays where you put it, and saving the alert saves it. The chain icon at"
" the left of the strip is linked while both handles follow the optical "
"picks. Once you move one, the chain is broken: select it (**Follow "
"optical**) to hand both handles back to the optical picks. A map whose "
"side has a radar image gets a **Radar** chip next to the **Optical** one "
"in its title: click a chip to choose what that map shows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2206
msgid "The toolbar above the track:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2216
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2572
msgid "Default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2217
msgid "**Image sources** button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2218
msgid ""
"Opens the menu of image sources, in two groups: **Optical** (Sentinel-2, "
"Landsat, Planet) and **Radar** (Sentinel-1). The button carries one "
"coloured dot for each source that is on. Each row has a checkbox, the "
"source's dot and name and, on the right, the number of its images in the "
"current view; a second line (\"3 over cloud limit\") appears when the "
"cloud limit hides some. Planet is greyed out, with \"No access with this "
"account\", when your GEE account has no NICFI access. The choice is saved"
" with the project (on a review copy, it lasts only for the session), and "
"opening an alert whose saved image comes from a source that is off turns "
"that source on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2219
msgid "Sentinel-2 and Landsat on; Planet and Sentinel-1 off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2220
msgid "**?** button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2221
msgid ""
"Shows or hides a short legend of the timeline. This section describes the"
" timeline in full."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2222
msgid "Hidden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2223
msgid "**Collapse the alert window**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2224
msgid ""
"Folds the months that lie wholly inside the alert window into blocks that"
" give their number of images. Select a block to unfold its month; select "
"a month's name on the axis to fold it. On a long alert, the folded months"
" share less than half of the track, so that the months before and after "
"the window keep their room. When they get too narrow to read, the folded "
"months of each half-year form one block (\"Jan – Jun 2024\") with the "
"year on the axis under it; select it to split it into one block per "
"month."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2225
msgid "Folded when an alert opens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2226
msgid "**Expand every month**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2227
msgid "Unfolds every month."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2229
msgid "**Max cloud**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2230
msgid ""
"The cloud limit, chosen in a menu of presets (10, 20, 40, 60 or 80 %, or "
"**All images**), each with the number of images it keeps on the timeline."
" Images over it are faded and never chosen automatically. Planet mosaics "
"and Sentinel-1 radar images have no cloud figure, so the limit never "
"hides them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2231
msgid "40 %."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2232
msgid "**Image area**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2233
msgid ""
"How far around the alert the images reach: **Normal**, **Large** or "
"**Extra large** (100 m, 1 km or 2.5 km around it). Larger areas take "
"longer to load and export. Saving the review saves the area: the alert "
"opens on it again, and its files and GIF are made on it. An alert never "
"saved opens on **Normal**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2234
msgid "**Normal**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2235
msgid "**+1 month** (left and right of the track)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2236
msgid ""
"Adds a month before or after the view. The right one stops at the current"
" month."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2239
msgid "Sentinel-1 radar images differ from the optical ones:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2241
msgid ""
"They are fetched only once you turn Sentinel-1 on for the project: until "
"its images are listed, its count reads \"–\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2242
msgid ""
"Both passes are shown, one band per pass, labelled \"Sentinel-1 asc\" and"
" \"Sentinel-1 desc\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2243
msgid ""
"They are shown raw, with no speckle filter, as VV, VH and the VV/VH ratio"
" in red, green and blue. In the map pane, a radar image has a single "
"\"Radar\" layer, with no true/false colour switch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2244
msgid ""
"Radar sees through clouds, so the cloud limit never hides these images. "
"They have their own lane and handles (see above): the radar handles "
"follow the optical picks until you move them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2245
msgid ""
"Both pairs are used as picked. With Sentinel-1 on, the zip holds two "
"composites, the optical one and the radar one, and the report adds a "
"*Radar evidence* row; the radar images that were not placed by hand are "
"marked in the report. The model and the GIF use the optical pair, "
"whatever the radar handles show. **Build files** waits until the radar "
"images are drawn and any radar handle you moved is saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2247
msgid ""
"The images come from an index of the images over the project's area, kept"
" on disk and refreshed after 24 hours. While it loads, the toolbar reads "
"\"Loading the image index…\"; an index older than a day reads \"Index "
"from (date)\". If a refresh fails, the index on screen keeps working, and"
" **Try again** retries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2254
msgid "The top of the panel shows what the alert table says:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2260
msgid "Row"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2264
msgid "**Detected**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2265
msgid "Its first and last detection dates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2266
msgid "**Status** row"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2267
msgid ""
"Its review status, with its colour: **Not reviewed**, **Reviewed: "
"confirmed**, **Reviewed: false positive** or **Reviewed: needs "
"revision**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2268
msgid "**Group**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2269
msgid ""
"For an alert reviewed with nearby alerts: \"group of 4\". Hidden "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2270
msgid "**Kind**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2271
msgid ""
"Whether the alert grows from earlier loss (see `Growth of earlier loss "
"<defo-integrate-growth_>`_): **Growth** (a purple chip), **Growth · under"
" minimum area**, or **New · under minimum area** (a small alert whose "
"links were all removed). Hidden for a new alert."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2272
msgid "**History**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2273
msgid ""
"For an alert linked to earlier loss: the alerts of its history and the "
"area they confirm, for example \"3 alerts · 2.1 ha confirmed since Aug "
"2026 (+0.3 ha not reviewed)\". The area counts once where shapes overlap."
" Hidden when the alert has no history."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2275
msgid ""
"If the active set is out of date or its files are missing, an orange line"
" above it says so, as in the `Overview <defo-overview_>`_. The review is "
"still possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2279
msgid "The review panel: verdict and questions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2283
msgid "Verdict"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2285
msgid "Under **Verdict**, select one of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2292
msgid "Stored status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2293
msgid "Use it when"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2294
msgid "**True alert**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2295
msgid "**Reviewed: confirmed**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2296
msgid "The images show forest loss where the alert is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2297
msgid "**False positive**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2298
msgid "**Reviewed: false positive**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2299
msgid "They show no forest loss: clouds, shadows, a seasonal change…"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2300
msgid "**Needs revision**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2301
msgid "**Reviewed: needs revision**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2302
msgid "No decision is possible yet, or the alert needs a second look."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2304
msgid ""
"An unreviewed alert opens with no verdict: nothing is chosen "
"automatically. A reviewed alert opens on its saved verdict and answers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2307
msgid "Questions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2309
msgid ""
"The **Questions** section holds the questions of the `questionnaire "
"<defo-questionnaire_>`_, in their order and numbered. Once a verdict is "
"chosen, it shows only the questions asked for that verdict. The section's"
" badge counts the answers (\"1 of 2 answered\") and turns orange when a "
"required question has no answer (\"1 of 2 · required missing\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2311
msgid "A question with one answer shows its options as tiles: select one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2312
msgid ""
"A question with several answers shows them as chips: select each one that"
" applies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2313
msgid ""
"A question that allows typed answers is a list that also accepts typing "
"(**Pick or type answers**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2315
msgid ""
"With no questions in the project, the section reads \"This project asks "
"no questions: add some in the Questionnaire step.\"; when the chosen "
"verdict asks none, \"No questions are asked for this verdict.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2317
msgid ""
"A **Required** tag marks a question that must be answered before saving. "
"The section starts open or closed as set by **Show the questions expanded"
" in Analysis** in the questionnaire. It opens by itself when the chosen "
"verdict asks a required question with no answer yet, and when a save is "
"refused for that reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2322
msgid "Refine the polygon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2324
msgid ""
"The alert's polygon comes from the alert pixels. In **Refine polygon**, "
"draw the area that was actually lost instead. The saved polygon is stored"
" with the review, shown as *Defo Layer* on the maps, and its area becomes"
" the alert's area. The section's badge reads \"nothing drawn\" or, for "
"example, \"2 shapes · 1.3 ha\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2328
msgid "Drawing the polygon of an alert"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2331
msgid "To refine the polygon:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2333
msgid ""
"Select **Start drawing**. Both maps switch to drawing mode, the alert's "
"box is hidden, and the saved polygon (if any) becomes the drawing, in "
"blue. **Stop drawing** takes the button's place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2334
msgid "Edit the drawing on either map; the other follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2336
msgid ""
"The polygon button in the upper-left corner draws a new shape: click on "
"its corners, then click on the first one to close it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2337
msgid ""
"Drag a corner to move it, click on the small marker in the middle of a "
"side to add a corner, and right-click a corner to delete it. An edit that"
" would make a shape cross itself is undone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2338
msgid ""
"The bin button deletes the next shape clicked. Its actions **Select "
"area** (drag a box around the shapes to delete) and **Clear all** ask for"
" confirmation first (\"Delete 2 shapes?\", **Cancel** / **Delete**), with"
" the shapes concerned in red. Press **Esc** to cancel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2339
msgid ""
"**Fill holes** removes the holes of the selected shape, or of every shape"
" when none is selected. **Remove hole**: click inside a hole to remove "
"it; press **Esc** or select the button again to stop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2341
msgid ""
"Select **Save drawing**. The drawing becomes the alert's polygon. A "
"drawing with no shape removes the polygon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2342
msgid ""
"Select **Stop drawing** to leave drawing mode. If the drawing has changes"
" not saved with **Save drawing**, the **Discard unsaved drawing?** dialog"
" asks first: **Keep drawing**, **Save and stop** or **Discard changes**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2346
msgid ""
"**Save drawing** does not save the review: select **Save** afterwards. "
"Until the drawing is saved, the footer reads \"Save your drawing before "
"saving this review\" and the review cannot be saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2349
msgid "The two models"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2351
msgid ""
"Under the drawing buttons, two convolutional neural networks (CNNs) can "
"find the loss on the before and after images on screen: **Model 1** "
"(\"Smaller and faster model\") and **Model 2** (\"Larger but slower "
"model\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2353
msgid "To use a model:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2355
msgid ""
"Select **Run** on a model's row. The app downloads the two images (the "
"area set by **Image area**) and runs the model. It takes a while; the run"
" shows in the task list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2356
msgid ""
"Read the result on the row (e.g. \"Found 3 patches · 2.1 ha\"). Patches "
"smaller than the set's **Minimum cluster size** are left out. When the "
"model found nothing, a red warning icon appears instead (\"Model did not "
"find forest loss polygons\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2357
msgid ""
"Select the map icon with a plus sign (**Add to map**) to add the patches "
"to the drawing (it starts drawing mode if needed): lime for **Model 1**, "
"purple for **Model 2**. The icon then turns into a minus sign (**Remove "
"from map**), which takes them off again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2358
msgid "Edit the result like any drawing, then select **Save drawing**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2360
msgid ""
"Choosing other images or another **Image area** drops the models' "
"results: run them again. If another alert is opened while a model runs, "
"its result is not added (\"The model finished after you moved to another "
"alert: its prediction was not added.\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2365
msgid "Earlier alerts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2367
msgid ""
"This section appears when the active set's period has earlier periods "
"with alert sets. It lists the earlier loss near the alert: the alerts of "
"earlier periods reviewed as **Reviewed: confirmed** or **Reviewed: needs "
"revision**, within the distance set in **Within**, in metres (100 m by "
"default, from 10 m to 50 km), plus every alert linked to this one, "
"however far. Use it to check whether an alert continues a clearing "
"already reported, and to link it to that clearing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2369
msgid "The alerts are grouped by period, newest first. Each row shows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2371
msgid "a bar in the period's colour;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2372
msgid "a box, ticked when the alert is linked to this one;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2373
msgid ""
"the earlier alert's number and area (\"#12 · 3.4 ha\"), and its status; "
"and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2374
msgid ""
"how it relates to this alert: \"touches\" (linked by `Integrate & "
"vectorize <defo-integrate-growth_>`_), \"touches · not linked\" (the link"
" was removed) or its distance (\"40 m\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2376
msgid "Select an alert's number to zoom both maps to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2378
msgid ""
"To link or unlink an alert, tick or clear its box. The change is part of "
"the review: the footer reads \"Unsaved changes on this alert\", and "
"**Save** saves it with the verdict. Ticking an alert of an earlier period"
" makes this alert a growth alert, even if it does not touch it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2380
msgid ""
"A growth alert smaller than the **Minimum cluster size** is in the set "
"only because of its link. Clearing its last link asks first (**Unlink "
"from the earlier alert?**): for example \"Alert #14 is 0.2 ha, under the "
"0.5 ha minimum. It is an alert only because it is linked to #12.\" Select"
" **Unlink** to clear the link: the alert stays in the set as **New · "
"under minimum area**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2382
msgid "Some rows have no box:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2384
msgid ""
"\"via #12\": the alert belongs to the history through another link (here,"
" alert 12). Clearing the box of alert 12 removes it too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2385
msgid ""
"\"earlier set was re-run\": the earlier alert's set was made again in "
"`Integrate & vectorize <defo-integrate-replace_>`_, so the link no longer"
" points at the same alert. The row is greyed, is not counted in the "
"history, and the link is dropped the next time this alert is saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2387
msgid ""
"A linked alert that was later reviewed as a false positive stays ticked "
"with \"now false positive\". It is greyed and left out of the history; "
"clear its box to remove the link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2389
msgid ""
"Turn on **Show on the maps** to outline the listed alerts on both maps. "
"The colour is the period's, and a small legend lists the periods shown, "
"with \"solid: confirmed · dashed: needs revision · thick: linked\". The "
"switch starts on for a growth alert; on other alerts it keeps your last "
"choice. When the list covers several periods, the **Periods** menu hides "
"some of them. The badge reads \"off\", \"none within 100 m\" or, for "
"example, \"4 within 100 m · 1 linked\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2391
msgid ""
"In a `review copy <defo-evaluation-return_>`_, the list comes from a "
"snapshot of the earlier alerts taken when the packages were built: the "
"section reads \"Earlier alerts as of (date)\", or \"No earlier alerts in "
"this copy\" for a package made by an older version of the app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2396
msgid "Nearby alerts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2398
msgid ""
"This section appears only when **Review nearby alerts together** is "
"selected in `Evaluation <defo-evaluation-group_>`_. One clearing often "
"makes several small alerts side by side. Review them together: one "
"verdict, one set of answers, one pair of images and one polygon for all "
"of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2400
msgid ""
"The section lists the alerts within the distance set in **Evaluation**, "
"measured edge to edge from the alert on screen: the ticked ones first, "
"then the nearest others, at most 50 (\"12 more in range not listed\"). "
"Each row shows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2402
msgid "a box, ticked when the alert is part of the next save;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2403
msgid ""
"the alert's number (select it to zoom both maps to it), its first "
"detection date and its area;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2404
msgid "its distance (\"40 m\"), or \"in this group\";"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2405
msgid "\"group #12\" when it belongs to another group;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2406
msgid "its status; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2407
msgid ""
"in a split set, \"assigned to Ana\", greyed and with no box, for an alert"
" of another evaluator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2409
msgid ""
"The list offers the alerts not reviewed and the alerts reviewed in a "
"group. Alerts reviewed before grouping was on are offered only with "
"**Include already reviewed alerts**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2411
msgid ""
"The listed alerts are outlined on both maps (*Nearby alerts* layer). "
"Click on a map near an outline to tick or clear that alert. **Select "
"all** ticks every listed alert and **Clear** clears them. The badge reads"
" \"3 selected\", \"5 within 300 m\" or \"none within 300 m\". When a "
"ticked alert lies outside the images, a line says \"Some selected alerts "
"are outside the image area: pick a larger area on the timeline.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2413
msgid "To review a group:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2415
msgid "Tick the alerts that show the same clearing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2416
msgid ""
"Give the verdict, answer the questions, choose the images and draw the "
"polygon as for one alert."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2417
msgid "Select **Save**, which then reads \"Save for 4 alerts\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2419
msgid ""
"When the save changes other reviews, the **Save this group?** dialog "
"lists them first, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2421
msgid "\"#15 (Reviewed: confirmed): its review is replaced\";"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2422
msgid ""
"\"#16 (Reviewed: confirmed): moves from group #9\" or \"joins with group "
"#9\" (a whole group joins when its main alert is ticked); and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2423
msgid ""
"\"#17 (Not reviewed): leaves the group and goes back to not reviewed\" "
"(an alert of this group left unticked)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2425
msgid "Select **Save** or **Cancel**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2427
msgid ""
"Every alert of the group gets the same verdict, answers, images and links"
" to earlier alerts. The alert on screen when the group is first saved is "
"its *main* alert: it keeps the drawn polygon. When the group has a "
"drawing, the other alerts get an area of 0, so that the loss counts once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2429
msgid ""
"An alert of a saved group opens with the banner \"Reviewed as a group of "
"4 (main alert #12)\", and the **Group** row of the panel reads \"group of"
" 4\". The *Original alert* layer outlines the whole group. On an alert "
"other than the main one, **Remove from group** takes it out of the group:"
" confirm with **Remove**. The alert goes back to not reviewed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2431
msgid ""
"A group needs one evaluator: \"These alerts are assigned to different "
"evaluators: a group needs one.\" In a review copy, only your own alerts "
"can join: \"Some of these alerts are not assigned to you.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2436
msgid "Save the review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2438
msgid ""
"The *dock* stays at the bottom of the panel: the **Export this alert** "
"section, then the buttons, then a state line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2446
msgid "**Save**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2447
msgid ""
"Saves the review and stays on the alert. With nearby alerts ticked, it "
"reads \"Save for 4 alerts\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2448
msgid "**Next**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2449
msgid "Opens the next alert (the next match under a filter)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2451
msgid "Opens the next alert without a verdict, as in the top bar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2453
msgid ""
"The filled button shows the next step: **Save** while the alert has "
"unsaved changes or no saved review, **Next** once the review is saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2455
msgid ""
"With unsaved changes, **Next**, the icon and the top bar's **Previous**, "
"**Next**, **Go** and icon ask first. The buttons give way to \"This alert"
" has unsaved changes\": **Discard** drops the changes and moves on, "
"**Stay** keeps you on the alert."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2457
msgid ""
"A change started somewhere else (a **Go** in **Overview** or in a map "
"popup, the alert set picked in **Overview**, or opening, creating, "
"renaming or deleting the open project in **Project**) asks in the "
"**Unsaved changes in Analysis** dialog, over the window you are in. "
"**Continue anyway** drops the changes and does what you selected; **Open "
"Analysis** cancels it and shows the alert, so you can save it. Closing "
"the dialog does nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2459
msgid ""
"The state line reads \"Unsaved changes on this alert\", \"Save your "
"drawing before saving this review\" or \"Saved 14:32\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2461
msgid "A save writes into the alert set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2463
msgid "the verdict, as the alert's status;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2464
msgid ""
"the answers to the questions asked for that verdict (the others are left "
"empty);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2465
msgid "the before and after images chosen, so that the alert reopens on them;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2466
msgid ""
"the polygon saved in **Refine polygon**, with its area as the alert's "
"area;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2467
msgid ""
"the earlier alerts ticked in `Earlier alerts <defo-analysis-earlier_>`_, "
"as the alert's links;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2468
msgid ""
"with nearby alerts ticked, the group (see `Nearby alerts <defo-analysis-"
"nearby_>`_);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2469
msgid ""
"who reviewed it and when: ``reviewed_by`` (your SEPAL user name, looked "
"up once per session; left empty if it is unknown) and ``reviewed_at`` "
"(the time, in UTC, e.g. ``2026-11-11T14:03:22Z``). A group's members get "
"them too, and an alert reset to not reviewed loses them; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2470
msgid ""
"the names of the administrative areas under the alert, if `Integrate & "
"vectorize <defo-integrate_>`_ could not fill them (from the FAO GAUL 2024"
" boundaries). Names saved by earlier reviews are kept. If the project has"
" no boundaries yet, the first such save downloads them once, and its "
"progress reads \"Fetching administrative boundaries for this project "
"(once)…\" meanwhile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2472
msgid ""
"``admin1`` is the country, ``admin2`` the first-level unit and ``admin3``"
" the second-level unit. In a group, each alert keeps its own names; the "
"group's single-alert file and report show all the names of the group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2474
msgid ""
"Reviews show at once in the progress bar, in the set selector and in the "
"`Overview <defo-overview_>`_. A review can change at any time: open the "
"alert, change it and save again."
msgstr ""

