#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2549
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2551
msgid ""
"The Overview sums up an alert set, or every period at once: how many "
"alerts it holds, how many are reviewed, and how much loss was confirmed, "
"where and when; how the source pixels became alerts; and the files to "
"download. Its figures follow the reviews as they are saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2554
msgid "Open the Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2556
msgid ""
"Select **Overview** in the left rail. It opens as a large dialog over the"
" map; close it with its cross. It shows the active alert set, or \"No "
"alert set yet. Run Integrate & vectorize to produce one.\" when the "
"project has none."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2560
msgid "The Overview dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2564
msgid "The header"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2574
msgid ""
"The set summed up. Choosing another one makes it the project's active "
"set, as in `Analysis <defo-analysis-topbar_>`_. Its first item, \"All "
"periods · 3 sets · 133 alerts\", sums the newest set of every period "
"instead, and leaves the active set as it is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2575
msgid "The active set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2576
msgid "**Area (ha)** / **Alert count**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2577
msgid "Whether every figure of the page counts hectares or alerts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2578
msgid "**Area (ha)**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2579
msgid "**Review alerts**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2580
msgid ""
"Closes the Overview and opens `Analysis <defo-analysis_>`_ on this set. "
"Disabled when the set has no alerts, and for **All periods** (\"Pick one "
"period to review its alerts\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2583
msgid ""
"If the set is out of date or its files are missing, an orange line says "
"so (\"This set was built from inputs that have changed since…\" or \"This"
" set's files are missing from the project folder…\"). The figures still "
"show what the set holds. Run `Integrate & vectorize <defo-integrate-"
"outdated_>`_ again to rebuild it, which discards its reviews."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2586
msgid "The key figures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2592
msgid "Figure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2594
msgid "**Confirmed loss**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2595
msgid ""
"The area (or number) of alerts reviewed as **Reviewed: confirmed**. With "
"an earlier period, it compares with that period, in the page's measure "
"(\"▼ 780 less than 2026-09-01 → 2026-09-30\", or \"▲ … more than …\"). "
"**All periods** has no comparison."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2596
msgid "**Detected in total**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2597
msgid "The area (or number) of all the set's alerts, whatever their status."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2598
msgid "**Reviewed**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2599
msgid ""
"The share of alerts that have a verdict, and \"16 of 48 alerts\". It "
"always counts alerts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2600
msgid "**Largest alert**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2601
msgid ""
"The largest alert's area, its number, its country and its date. It always"
" counts hectares. The country shows for every alert of a set made with "
"this version; in a set made before, once the alert is saved. The number "
"is the alert's number: in a set made with this version, the same as the "
"Analysis counter's number (a set made before numbers from 0, so it is the"
" counter's number minus one)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2606
msgid "Map layers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2608
msgid ""
"The **Map layers** button beside **Review alerts** opens a list of the "
"layers the Overview can draw on the main map, grouped by period. Tick a "
"layer to draw it: the Overview closes, to show the map. Clear it to take "
"the layer off. Every layer is named with its period (\"Alerts · "
"2026-01-01 → 2026-01-31\"), in the list, on the map and in the legend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2610
msgid ""
"**This set**: the selected set's **Alerts**, coloured by status, and its "
"not-analysable pixels (too small, or over the alert cap), when the set's "
"run recorded them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2611
msgid ""
"**Other periods**: the alerts of every other period's newest set, newest "
"period first, each on its own. When there are several, **Show all** and "
"**Hide all** draw or clear them together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2612
msgid ""
"With **All periods** selected, **Every period** lists the alerts and the "
"not-analysable pixels of each period's newest set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2614
msgid "A layer's box is greyed while the layer is being built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2619
msgid "The tabs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2621
msgid "The figures are grouped in tabs, each with two cards side by side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2625
msgid "The Overview figures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2632
msgid "Tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2633
msgid "Cards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2635
msgid ""
"**By review status**: one bar split by status, then a table with, per "
"status, the number of alerts, their area, their share of the measure and "
"the median alert size, and a **Total** row. **How big the alerts are**: "
"the alerts by size, from under 0.5 ha to 25 ha or more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2636
msgid "**Over time**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2637
msgid ""
"**Across monitoring periods**: one column per monitoring period of the "
"project, split by status, from its newest alert set; a period still under"
" review shows its unreviewed share hatched. With one period only, it "
"reads \"This project has one monitoring period. Add a second one and its "
"trend is charted here.\" **When the loss was detected**: the alerts by "
"the week they were first detected, split by status. Hatched weeks are "
"look-back weeks: they fall before the period started (see `What earlier "
"periods already reported <defo-integrate-earlier_>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2638
msgid "**Place & source**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2639
msgid ""
"**By administrative area**: the reviewed alerts by area, up to eight, the"
" most confirmed loss first: their **Area (ha)**, the hectares **Reviewed:"
" confirmed** and the number of **Alerts**. **Country** or **Province / "
"state** sets the level; a province is shown with its country (\"Peru › "
"Madre de Dios\"). The areas come from the FAO GAUL 2024 boundaries, "
"recorded for every alert by `Integrate & vectorize <defo-integrate_>`_, "
"but only reviewed alerts are counted; an alert with none recorded is "
"counted as **Not recorded**, and an alert across a border is listed under"
" every area it falls in. **By alert source**: the alerts by the "
"combination of sources that detected them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2640
msgid "**Answers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2641
msgid ""
"One card per `question <defo-questionnaire_>`_, with the answers given to"
" reviewed alerts: the five most frequent, then **Other** and **No "
"answer**. An alert with two answers counts under each. Only shown when "
"the project has questions; the tab shows their number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2642
msgid "**Pixels**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2643
msgid "How the pixels of the sources became the pixels of the alerts (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2644
msgid "**Clusters**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2645
msgid ""
"How those pixels became alerts, the nearby alerts and the alerts linked "
"to earlier loss (see below). The tab shows the number of alerts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2646
msgid "**Files**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2647
msgid ""
"The **Export alerts** card (see `The whole set, from the Overview <defo-"
"export-set_>`_) and, with **All periods** selected, the **Summary of all "
"periods** (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2649
msgid ""
"When a figure cannot be drawn, its card reads \"This figure could not be "
"drawn; its numbers are below.\" and lists them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2652
msgid "Pixels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2654
msgid ""
"The **From source pixels to alert pixels** card follows the pixels step "
"by step, each with a bar, a number and its hectares:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2656
msgid ""
"**Source alert pixels**: the pixels the sources flagged in the period, "
"all sources together;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2657
msgid ""
"**Removed by masks** and **Kept by the masks**: what the masks of "
"`Harmonize <defo-harmonize_>`_ took out and left;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2658
msgid ""
"**Combined, overlaps once**: the pixels once the sources are combined, a "
"pixel flagged by two sources counted once;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2659
msgid ""
"**Too small to analyse** and **Over the alert limit**: the pixels of "
"clusters below the minimum area, and of clusters left out by the alert "
"limit of `Integrate & vectorize <defo-integrate_>`_; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2660
msgid "**In alerts**: the pixels of the set's alerts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2662
msgid ""
"The **By source** card gives the same counts per source (**Alert px**, "
"**Masked**, **Kept**), each with an eye that draws the source's raster on"
" the map, and the **Masks used** with their **Mode**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2664
msgid ""
"A count shows \"—\" when the set was made before the app recorded it: "
"\"—: not recorded for this set. Run Integrate & vectorize again to count "
"it.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2669
msgid "Clusters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2671
msgid ""
"The **From clusters to alerts** card counts the **Clusters formed** by "
"connected alert pixels, those **Under the minimum size** and **Over the "
"alert limit**, the **Alerts** made from the rest, and how many are "
"**Reviewed**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2673
msgid ""
"Under it, **Nearby alerts** shows how the set's alerts chain into groups:"
" alerts within the distance of **Review nearby alerts together** (see "
"`Evaluation <defo-evaluation-group_>`_), edge to edge, form one group. "
"Its table has two rows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2675
msgid ""
"**Found by distance**: the groups the distance makes, and their alerts "
"(\"20 of 48 · largest 5\"); and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2676
msgid ""
"**Saved as a review group**: the groups saved in Analysis, and their "
"alerts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2678
msgid ""
"When grouping is off, the card uses the project's distance and adds "
"\"Reviewing together is off · turn it on in Evaluation.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2680
msgid ""
"The **Linked to earlier loss** card follows the `growth alerts <defo-"
"integrate-growth_>`_: new alerts that touch a clearing confirmed in an "
"earlier period (draw the earlier sets from `Map layers <defo-overview-"
"layers_>`_). Its headline gives the growth alerts and their area (\"3 "
"growth alerts · 4.2 ha\", or only the number with **Alert count**); the "
"line under it splits them (\"Growth: 2 · Under minimum area: 1\") and "
"says how many are reviewed. Without any, it reads \"No alert is linked to"
" earlier loss.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2682
msgid ""
"Its table lists the histories that include an alert of this set, the "
"largest confirmed area first:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2690
msgid "**Monitoring periods**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2691
msgid "The first and the last period of the history."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2693
msgid "The number of alerts in the history, all periods together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2694
msgid "**Confirmed (ha)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2695
msgid ""
"The area of the history's alerts reviewed as **Reviewed: confirmed** or "
"**Reviewed: needs revision**, counted once where their shapes overlap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2696
msgid "**This set adds (ha)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2697
msgid "The area of this set's alerts in the history, false positives left out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2698
msgid "**Review**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2699
msgid ""
"Closes the Overview and opens this set's alert of the history in "
"`Analysis <defo-analysis_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2702
msgid "Summary of all periods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2704
msgid ""
"With **All periods** selected, the **Files** tab ends with a table of "
"every period, one row each: its **Alerts**, **Confirmed ha**, "
"**Reviewed** share, **Source px**, **Clusters**, review **Groups** and "
"alerts **Linked** to earlier loss. The **Summary CSV** tile under it "
"writes the same table to ``periods_summary.csv`` in the project folder; "
"select it again to download the file. When the numbers have changed since"
" (reviews saved, a set rebuilt), the tile reads \"Numbers changed since\""
" and an **Update** button writes it again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2707
msgid "All periods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2709
msgid ""
"Choose **All periods** in the **Alert set** selector to sum the newest "
"set of every period: the key figures, the tabs and the export then cover "
"them all. Hectares and alerts are added up; a pixel count that one set "
"did not record shows \"—\". **Map layers** lists every period's layers "
"(see `Map layers <defo-overview-layers_>`_); **Review alerts** needs one "
"set, so it is disabled. In the **Files** tab, the **Export alerts** card "
"writes every period's alerts to one file, with a ``period`` column (see "
"`The whole set, from the Overview <defo-export-set_>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2714
msgid "\"No alert set yet. Run Integrate & vectorize to produce one.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2715
msgid "The project has no set: run `Integrate & vectorize <defo-integrate_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2717
msgid "\"This set has no alerts.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2718
msgid "The set was made but found no alert; nothing is charted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2720
msgid "\"This set's alerts could not be read: …\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2721
msgid ""
"The set's files are damaged or missing. Run `Integrate & vectorize <defo-"
"integrate_>`_ again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2723
msgid ""
"\"No reviewed alert answered this yet.\" or \"No alert has been reviewed "
"yet, so no administrative area is on record.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2724
msgid "Review alerts in `Analysis <defo-analysis_>`_ to fill these cards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2729
msgid "Export"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2731
msgid "The app exports alerts in two ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2733
msgid "the files of one reviewed alert, from the Analysis screen; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2734
msgid "the alerts of a whole set, or of every period, from the Overview."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2736
msgid ""
"Every file is written into the alert set's folder in the project "
"(``periods/<start>_<end>/sets/<set>/``, see `Project <defo-project_>`_), "
"so it can also be found there later, in SEPAL's file browser. The files "
"of **All periods** go to the project folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2741
msgid "One alert, from Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2743
msgid ""
"The **Export this alert** section sits at the top of the dock of the "
"`Analysis <defo-analysis-save_>`_ review panel. It works on the alert on "
"screen, once its review is saved: its badge reads \"available after "
"save\", then \"ready to build\", then \"3 files ready\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2747
msgid "The alert's files, ready to download"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2754
#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2831
msgid "Tile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2756
msgid "**Build files**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2757
msgid ""
"Builds the alert's data and report from the saved review (\"Makes the "
"files above from the saved review\"). It is disabled until the review on "
"screen is saved: it then reads \"Save this alert first\", or \"Save your "
"changes first\" when there are unsaved changes. A reviewed alert opened "
"on the images it was saved with is ready at once. It runs in the task "
"list (\"Building files…\") and takes a while: it downloads the before and"
" after images."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2758
msgid "**Alert data**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2759
msgid ""
"Downloads a .zip file: the alert's GeoPackage, its before and after "
"images as one GeoTIFF (two with Sentinel-1 on: optical and radar) and, "
"for a true alert, its GIF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2760
msgid "**Alert report**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2761
msgid "Downloads the alert's Word report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2762
msgid "**Rebuild files**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2763
msgid "Builds the files again (e.g. after the review changed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2764
msgid "**Timelapse**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2765
msgid ""
"Makes and downloads an animated GIF of the alert (see below). For an "
"alert not saved as a true alert, it reads \"True alerts only\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2767
msgid ""
"The files are named after the alert's number (``<n>``). In a set made "
"with this version, it starts at 1 and is the counter's number. A set made"
" before keeps its numbers, which start at 0, and its file names "
"(``alert_0``…):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2773
msgid "File"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2775
msgid "``alert_<n>.gpkg``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2776
msgid ""
"The alert as one feature with its attributes and answers (the answers in "
"the app's current language). Its geometry is the polygon drawn in `Refine"
" the polygon <defo-analysis-refine_>`_, or else the alert's cluster "
"polygon, never the bounding box. ``geometry_source`` says which "
"(``drawn`` or ``detected``; ``group`` is explained below), and "
"``detected_area_ha`` is the cluster's area as detected, while ``area_ha``"
" stays the reviewed area. A second layer, ``alert_<n>_detected``, holds "
"the cluster polygon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2777
msgid "``alert_<n>_<before>_<after>.tif``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2778
msgid ""
"The before and after images, cut to the **Image area**. The two date "
"parts name each image's collection (``s`` Sentinel-2, ``l`` Landsat, "
"``p`` Planet, ``a``/``d`` Sentinel-1 ascending/descending) and date. With"
" Sentinel-1 on there are two: the optical pair and the radar pair, each "
"as picked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2779
msgid "``alert_<n>_<before>_<after>.gif``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2780
msgid "The timelapse, when made, named like the GeoTIFF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2781
msgid "``alert_<n>.zip``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2782
msgid "The GeoPackage, the GeoTIFF (or the two) and, for a true alert, the GIF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2783
msgid "``alert_<n>.docx``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2784
msgid "The Word report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2786
msgid ""
"For an alert of a group (see `Nearby alerts <defo-analysis-nearby_>`_), "
"the files describe the whole group: the GeoPackage holds one feature with"
" the group's summed area, its first and last detection dates, its "
"sources, ``group_size`` (the number of alerts) and ``group_alerts`` "
"(their numbers, e.g. \"12, 15, 16\"), and the GIF outlines every alert of"
" the group. Its geometry is the group's drawn polygon; without one, it is"
" the union of the group's clusters (``geometry_source`` ``detected``). "
"The ``_detected`` layer holds that union of clusters. The administrative "
"names of the file and the report are all those of the group's alerts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2788
msgid ""
"The links of the tiles are for the review on screen. Choosing other "
"images, saving the alert again or changing the report template hides "
"them: build the files again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2791
msgid "The report"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2793
msgid ""
"The report is built from the project's Word template, chosen in the "
"`Questionnaire <defo-questionnaire-template_>`_ step, or from the app's "
"default template when the project has none. The template's placeholders "
"are filled with the alert's attributes, its answers and its images. With "
"Sentinel-1 on, the pictures show the optical pair as picked, a *Radar "
"evidence* row shows the radar pair, and the summary names both the "
"optical and the radar images. See `The report template <defo-"
"questionnaire-template_>`_ for the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2796
msgid "The timelapse"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2798
msgid ""
"The **Timelapse** tile makes an animated GIF that runs through the images"
" of the alert's area, from before to after, with the alert's outline over"
" them. Each frame stays 2 seconds and is labelled with its collection and"
" date. The before and after frames also name their side (\"Before · "
"Sentinel-2 2026-07-28\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2800
msgid ""
"It is offered for a true alert only: the tile is active when the alert is"
" saved as **Reviewed: confirmed** and the images on screen are those it "
"was saved with. Otherwise, it reads \"Save as a true alert, with the "
"images on screen, to create it\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2802
msgid "The frames are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2804
msgid "the before and after images chosen in the review; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2805
msgid ""
"up to two images before the before image and two after the after image, "
"found within 12 months, under the timeline's **Max cloud** limit and "
"never a Planet mosaic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2807
msgid ""
"The GIF is saved next to the other files and, when the alert's files are "
"built, added to the .zip file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2812
msgid "The whole set, from the Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2814
msgid ""
"The **Export alerts** card, in the **Files** tab of the `Overview <defo-"
"overview_>`_, writes the alerts of the set shown to a single file. Its "
"top line sums up the alerts that the chosen **Alerts** chip writes, with "
"the set's sources and dates (e.g. \"11 alerts · 304.9 ha · GLAD-L + "
"GLAD-S2 + RADD · 2026-10-01 – 2026-10-20\" for **Confirmed**). The folder"
" chip next to it copies the folder's path when selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2818
msgid "The Export alerts card of the Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2821
msgid "To export the set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2823
msgid ""
"Choose the alerts to write with the **Alerts** chips: **Confirmed**, "
"**All reviewed**, **Not reviewed** or **All**. Each chip shows its number"
" of alerts; a chip with none is disabled. **Confirmed** is chosen first "
"when the set has confirmed alerts, **All** otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2824
msgid ""
"Select a format tile to write the file. It reads \"Writing 11 alerts…\" "
"while it works, and the task list shows **Exporting alerts**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2825
msgid ""
"Select the tile again, now a download link with the time it was written, "
"to download the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2833
msgid "**GeoPackage**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2834
msgid ""
"One polygon per alert, with its attributes and answers, in a layer named "
"after the file. The geometry is what the reviewer approved: the polygon "
"drawn in Analysis if there is one, else the alert's cluster polygon, "
"never the bounding box. A second layer, ``<name>_detected``, holds the "
"cluster polygons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2835
msgid "**CSV table**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2836
msgid ""
"One row per alert with every column, geometries written as well-known "
"text (WKT): ``geometry`` is the reviewed shape and ``detected_geometry``,"
" next to it, the cluster polygon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2838
msgid ""
"Both files add the columns ``geometry_source`` (``drawn``, ``detected`` "
"or ``group``) and ``detected_area_ha`` (the cluster's area as detected; "
"``area_ha`` is the reviewed area). A member of a group whose main alert "
"has a drawing has no shape of its own: its ``geometry_source`` is "
"``group`` and its ``review_group`` names the main alert whose drawing "
"covers it. Both files also carry ``reviewed_by`` and ``reviewed_at`` (see"
" `Save the review <defo-analysis-save_>`_) and add three columns on "
"`growth <defo-integrate-growth_>`_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2840
msgid ""
"``kind``: ``new``, ``growth``, ``growth_small`` or ``new_small`` (see "
"**Kind** in `The review panel <defo-analysis-panel_>`_);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2841
msgid ""
"``grows_from``: the alert's links, separated by \";\", each written as "
"*set*\\ ``#``\\ *alert number*\\ ``@``\\ *run of that set*; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2842
msgid ""
"``history_area_ha``: the confirmed area of the alert's history, 0 for an "
"alert without one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2844
msgid ""
"The file is named after the set's sources, its period and the chosen "
"alerts (e.g. "
"``alerts_glad-l-glad-s2-radd_2026-08-01_2026-09-30_confirmed.gpkg``): "
"``_reviewed`` for **All reviewed**, ``_unreviewed`` for **Not reviewed**,"
" and no suffix for **All**. The card's last line shows the name. Answers "
"are written in the app's current language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2846
msgid ""
"With **All periods** chosen in the **Alert set** selector, the card "
"writes every period's alerts to one file in the project folder, with a "
"``period`` column giving each alert's period. Its name joins the sources "
"of every set and runs from the first period's start to the last period's "
"end (e.g. ``alerts_glad-l_2026-08-01_2026-10-23.gpkg``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2848
msgid ""
"When reviews are saved after a file was written, its tile reads **Reviews"
" changed since**, with an **Update** button. Select it to write the file "
"again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2853
msgid ""
"\"The before and after images for this alert are not both ready, so its "
"files cannot be built.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2854
msgid ""
"Choose both images on the timeline and let the two maps finish drawing "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2856
msgid ""
"\"No alert set is active, so there is nowhere in the project to save the "
"alert files. Run Integrate & vectorize first.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2857
msgid "Run `Integrate & vectorize <defo-integrate_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2859
msgid ""
"\"The report template … is gone. Pick it again in the Questionnaire step,"
" or clear it to use the default template.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2860
msgid ""
"The project's template was moved or deleted: see `The report template "
"<defo-questionnaire-template_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2862
msgid ""
"\"The alert files are ready, but the GIF could not be made, so the zip "
"has no GIF.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2863
msgid "Try the **Timelapse** tile on its own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2865
msgid ""
"\"The before and after images are the same image, so the GIF would show "
"no change.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2866
msgid "Choose two different images on the timeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2868
msgid ""
"\"Fewer than two images could be rendered for this alert, so no GIF was "
"made.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2869
msgid "Choose other before and after images, then try again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2871
msgid ""
"\"The alert files finished building after you moved to another alert: "
"they were not offered for download here.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2872
msgid "Go back to the alert: the files are in the set folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2877
msgid "Use case: alert review in Madre de Dios, Peru"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2881
msgid ""
"This use case follows a small forest-monitoring team through two monthly "
"rounds in the department of Madre de Dios, in the Peruvian Amazon, on the"
" borders with Brazil and Bolivia. Gold mining and the spread of "
"agriculture both put pressure on its forest, so the team wants to know "
"each month where forest was lost, and why."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2883
msgid "The team has:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2885
msgid "a coordinator, who sets up the project and reviews alerts; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2886
msgid ""
"two evaluators, Ana and Luis, who review their share of the alerts from "
"their own SEPAL accounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2890
msgid ""
"The values in this use case come from the demo project the screenshots of"
" this article are taken from. The verdicts and answers show how the app "
"records a review; they are examples, not a checked assessment of the "
"forest in Madre de Dios."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2896
msgid "Set up the project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2898
msgid "The coordinator sets up the project as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2900
msgid ""
"**Project**: in the app, select **New project** and name it "
"``madre_de_dios`` (see `Create a project <defo-project-create_>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2901
msgid ""
"**AOI**: in the `AOI <defo-aoi_>`_ step, choose **Admin level 1**, then "
"Peru, then \"Madre De Dios\" (as the list spells it), and select **Select"
" AOI**. The area is saved as ``PER_Madre_De_Dios``. A whole department is"
" a large area: every later step takes longer than for a district."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2904
msgid "The September round"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2907
msgid "Period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2909
msgid "In `Monitoring period <defo-period_>`_, the coordinator:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2911
msgid "selects **New period**;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2912
msgid "sets the dates from 2026-09-01 to 2026-09-30;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2913
msgid ""
"enters 90 in **Look-back (days)** (a new project's first period starts at"
" 0); and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2914
msgid "selects **Add period**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2916
msgid ""
"The search window runs from 2026-06-03 to 2026-09-30, so clusters that "
"started between June and August, and alerts the sources published late, "
"are found too. As the first period, it has no earlier set: every alert in"
" its search window is kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2919
msgid "Alerts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2921
msgid ""
"In `Alert sources <defo-alerts_>`_, the coordinator adds the three "
"predefined sources: **GLAD-L (Landsat, 30 m)**, **RADD (Sentinel-1, 10 "
"m)** and **GLAD-S2 (Sentinel-2, 10 m)**, each with **Add to new periods**"
" left selected, so that the next periods start with them. Each one covers"
" the whole AOI. Under RADD, the app notes that it detects only in primary"
" humid tropical forest: elsewhere in the department, only GLAD-L and "
"GLAD-S2 can report alerts. Then the **Download** of each row downloads "
"the three sources over the search window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2926
msgid "In `Harmonize <defo-harmonize_>`_, the coordinator:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2928
msgid ""
"keeps the suggested grid, the UTM zone of the department (``EPSG:32719``)"
" at 10 m, and selects **Save grid**. The grid is 41425 × 38561 pixels, "
"about 12.8 GB per source before compression, so the app warns that the "
"downloads will take a while;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2929
msgid ""
"adds a mask so that only alerts in forest count: **Add mask**, the Hansen"
" Global Forest Change image "
"``UMD/hansen/global_forest_change_2025_v1_13``, band ``treecover2000``, "
"named ``forest_2000``, mode **Keep**; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2930
msgid ""
"selects the mask's **Align** and, once the mask reads \"Ready\", "
"**Harmonize** on each source's row, which harmonizes the three sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2932
msgid ""
"Downloading and harmonizing took about 15 minutes. The mask and each "
"source then read \"Ready\": GLAD-L with 2362718 alert pixels, RADD with "
"1508527 and GLAD-S2 with 1462458."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2937
msgid "In `Integrate & vectorize <defo-integrate_>`_, the coordinator:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2939
msgid "keeps the three sources and **Include probable (unconfirmed) alerts** on;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2940
msgid ""
"sets **Minimum cluster size** to 1 ha and **Order** to **Bigger clusters "
"first**; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2941
msgid ""
"selects **Limit the number of clusters**, with **Maximum number of "
"clusters** set to 48: the team can review about 48 alerts a month, so it "
"starts with the biggest ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2943
msgid ""
"The run makes the alert set \"2026-09-01 → 2026-09-30 · GLAD-L + GLAD-S2 "
"+ RADD\" with 48 alerts, from 383.18 ha down to 27.84 ha: 2870 ha in all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2945
msgid ""
"The clusters beyond the cap are kept as not analysable. The next period "
"reconsiders them only if its look-back reaches back into September and it"
" uses the same sources. October's 90-day look-back does (see `What "
"earlier periods already reported <defo-integrate-earlier_>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2950
msgid ""
"With the alert set built, **Set up review** unlocks. To judge alerts "
"against a recent image, the coordinator adds one `additional layer <defo-"
"layers_>`_: an **Earth Engine** Sentinel-2 image of 27 September 2026 "
"(tile 19LDF, east of Puerto Maldonado), drawn as an **RGB composite** in "
"**True colour** (B4, B3, B2), **Min** 0 and **Max** 3000, named "
"``Sentinel-2 2026-09-27``, and **Show in Analysis** selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2954
msgid ""
"Planet NICFI monthly mosaics would cover the whole department, but the "
"account used for this article has no NICFI access. This is why Planet is "
"greyed out in the **Image sources** menu of the Analysis timeline in the "
"screenshots below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2957
msgid "Review alone, then together"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2960
msgid "First reviews"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2962
msgid ""
"Before sharing the work, the coordinator opens `Analysis <defo-"
"analysis_>`_ and reviews the two biggest alerts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2964
msgid ""
"alert 1 (383.18 ha) as **True alert**, with the loss driver **Mining**; "
"and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2965
msgid "alert 2 (146.97 ha) as **False positive**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2970
msgid ""
"In `Evaluation <defo-evaluation_>`_, the coordinator selects **Multiple "
"evaluators**, then **Split alerts…**, chooses **Names**, enters Ana and "
"Luis, and selects **Split**. The alerts are dealt out in turn: Ana and "
"Luis get 23 each, and the two alerts already reviewed stay "
"**Unassigned**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2973
msgid "Before the packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2975
msgid ""
"The coordinator goes on reviewing in the original project while the split"
" is set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2977
msgid "alert 3 as **True alert**, with **Agriculture expansion**;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2978
msgid "alert 4 as **Needs revision**, with **Logging**; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2979
msgid "alert 5 as **True alert**, with **Mining**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2981
msgid ""
"These verdicts travel in the packages, so the evaluators see them; alerts"
" 3 and 5 are among Ana's. The coordinator then selects **Generate "
"packages** and sends each evaluator their .zip file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2987
msgid "Ana's review copy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2989
msgid ""
"Ana copies the package into her SEPAL folder and imports it with "
"**Import** in the `Project <defo-project-import_>`_ dialog. It opens as "
"the project ``madre-de-dios__e01-ana``, on the Analysis screen, already "
"filtered to her alerts (\"Evaluator: Ana\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2991
msgid "Ana works through them with **Save** and **Next**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2993
msgid ""
"the top bar counts \"5 reviewed · 18 left · filtered · 48 total\" (the "
"coordinator's two reviews of her alerts and three of her own);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2994
msgid "the counter numbers her alerts from 1 to 23; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2995
msgid ""
"her third alert, for example, is saved as **True alert** with **Mining**:"
" the after image shows bare, sandy ground with a green pond at the edge "
"of the forest, which looks like the pits that alluvial gold mining "
"leaves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:2999
msgid "Ana's review copy on the Analysis screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3002
msgid ""
"When done for now, Ana selects **Generate reviewed copy** in the "
"`Evaluation <defo-evaluation-return_>`_ step (\"5 / 23 of your alerts "
"reviewed\") and sends the ``__reviewed.zip`` file back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3005
msgid "Merge Ana's reviews"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3007
msgid ""
"The coordinator copies the file into the SEPAL folder, selects **Merge "
"reviewed copy…** and chooses it. The preview reads \"Ana: 3 new reviews, "
"1 conflicts, 1 unchanged, 0 ignored\":"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3009
msgid ""
"the unchanged review is alert 3, which Ana left as the coordinator saved "
"it; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3010
msgid ""
"the conflict is alert 5: the coordinator had confirmed it as mining, "
"while Ana marked it as a false positive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3012
msgid ""
"The coordinator keeps the original verdict with **Keep mine**, and plans "
"to look at that alert again with Ana. After **Merge**, the evaluators "
"table shows Ana with five of her 23 alerts reviewed and the date of the "
"merge (see `Merge a reviewed copy <defo-evaluation-merge_>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3015
msgid "Add a question"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3017
msgid ""
"The team also wants to record whether each clearing has an access road "
"nearby. In the `Questionnaire <defo-questionnaire_>`_ step, after the "
"default **Loss driver**, the coordinator adds a second question:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3019
msgid "**Add question**;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3020
msgid "\"Access road nearby?\";"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3021
msgid "**One answer**, with the options Yes and No;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3022
msgid "**Required** on; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3023
msgid "asked for **True alert** and **Needs revision** only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3025
msgid ""
"Because the questionnaire changed after the packages were built, their "
"cloud icons in `Evaluation <defo-evaluation-packages_>`_ turn amber. "
"Packages already sent still merge, by question key. For the new question "
"to reach the evaluators, the coordinator selects **Regenerate packages** "
"and sends the new ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3027
msgid ""
"From then on, a true alert or an alert that needs review gets both "
"answers (a false positive gets neither: both questions are asked only for"
" the other two verdicts). For example, alert 10 is saved as **True "
"alert**, with **Agriculture expansion** as the loss driver and \"No\" for"
" the access road. Its status reads **Reviewed: confirmed**, and the "
"**Questions** section reads \"2 of 2 answered\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3031
msgid "A reviewed alert: its verdict and its two answers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3034
msgid ""
"Back in the workflow, **Show these alerts on the map** in `Integrate & "
"vectorize <defo-integrate-map_>`_ draws the set over the department. At "
"this zoom, each alert is a dot coloured by its review status:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3036
msgid "grey for **Not reviewed**;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3037
msgid "red for **Reviewed: confirmed**;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3038
msgid "green for **Reviewed: false positive**; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3039
msgid "amber for **Reviewed: needs revision**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3041
msgid ""
"With 13 of the 48 alerts reviewed, most dots are still grey. Most alerts "
"lie in the south of the department."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3045
msgid ""
"The September alerts on the map of Madre de Dios, coloured by review "
"status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3049
msgid "The October round"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3051
msgid ""
"At the start of the next round, the coordinator selects **New period** in"
" `Monitoring period <defo-period-add_>`_. The dialog is pre-filled: from "
"2026-10-01 (the day after September ends) to today, with the 90 days of "
"look-back used last time. The coordinator sets the end to 2026-10-20, the"
" day of this round. **Add period** makes it the active period, with the "
"September period's mask choices and the three sources marked **Add to new"
" periods**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3053
msgid "Then:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3055
msgid ""
"each row's **Download** in `Alerts <defo-alerts_>`_ downloads the three "
"sources for the new window, and each row's **Harmonize** in `Harmonize "
"<defo-harmonize_>`_ harmonizes them; the grid and the mask are already "
"there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3056
msgid ""
"In `Integrate & vectorize <defo-integrate_>`_, the coordinator uses the "
"same settings as in September (1 ha, the 48 biggest alerts). Before "
"grouping the pixels into alerts, the run removes every pixel inside "
"September's 48 alerts, so that nothing is reported twice. The new set "
"holds 48 alerts again, for 1177 ha. None of them touches an alert "
"confirmed in September, so the run links none to earlier loss (see "
"`Growth of earlier loss <defo-integrate-growth_>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3058
msgid ""
"The team reviews them as in September; 16 are reviewed so far, 11 of them"
" as true alerts. With **Show these alerts on the map** and **Show earlier"
" sets** both on, the map shows the October alerts next to September's, "
"which are drawn in fainter colours. The October alerts lie in the same "
"parts of the department as September's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3062
msgid "The October alerts and the September alerts on the map"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3066
msgid "Read the figures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3068
msgid ""
"The `Overview <defo-overview_>`_ sums up the October set. In **Area "
"(ha)**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3070
msgid ""
"**Confirmed loss**: 305 ha, with \"▼ 780 less than 2026-09-01 → "
"2026-09-30\";"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3071
msgid "**Detected in total**: 1177 ha;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3072
msgid "**Reviewed**: 33 %, \"16 of 48 alerts\"; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3073
msgid ""
"**Largest alert**: 31.9 ha, the card's \"Alert 1\". In a set made with "
"this version, the Overview and the Analysis counter share the same "
"numbers, so this is the first alert there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3077
msgid "The key figures of the October set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3082
msgid ""
"The comparison needs care. **Confirmed loss** counts only the alerts "
"reviewed as true alerts, and only a third of the October alerts are "
"reviewed; the September figure, too, covers only the September alerts "
"reviewed so far. The arrow means that less loss is *confirmed* so far, "
"not that less forest was lost: the figure grows as the team goes on "
"reviewing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3084
msgid ""
"In the **Over time** tab, **Across monitoring periods** shows the two "
"periods side by side, with the share still under review hatched (2870 ha "
"detected in September, 1177 ha in October)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3086
msgid "In the **Answers** tab:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3088
msgid ""
"the card of the loss-driver question splits the reviewed area by answer "
"(in October: Mining first, then Agriculture expansion); and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3089
msgid ""
"the card of the new question splits it by its answers (in October: all "
"\"No\", 358 ha, with 81.2 ha under \"No answer\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3091
msgid "See `The tabs <defo-overview-figures_>`_ for every card."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3094
msgid "Share the results"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3097
msgid "The whole set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3099
msgid ""
"In the **Files** tab of the Overview, the **Export alerts** card writes "
"the October set to a file. The coordinator chooses **Confirmed** (11 "
"alerts, 304.9 ha) and selects the **GeoPackage** tile. The file "
"``alerts_glad-l-glad-s2-radd_2026-10-01_2026-10-20_confirmed.gpkg`` holds"
" one polygon per confirmed alert with its attributes and both answers, "
"ready for a GIS. The **CSV table** tile writes the same alerts as a table"
" for a spreadsheet. See `The whole set, from the Overview <defo-export-"
"set_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3102
msgid "One alert"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3104
msgid ""
"To report on one alert, the coordinator opens it in Analysis, saves it, "
"and selects **Build files** under **Export this alert**. The result is a "
".zip file with the alert's GeoPackage and its before and after images, "
"and a Word report built from the project's template. For a true alert, "
"the **Timelapse** tile also makes an animated GIF of the images from "
"before to after. See `One alert, from Analysis <defo-export-alert_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3106
msgid ""
"Every file is also kept in the alert set's folder of the project, under "
"``periods/2026-10-01_2026-10-20/sets/glad-l-glad-s2-radd/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3109
msgid "Next month"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3111
msgid "For the next round, the team plans to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3113
msgid ""
"select **New period** again: the dates continue the series, and the look-"
"back brings back the clusters set aside as too small the month before, so"
" a slowly growing clearing becomes an alert once it reaches 1 ha, without"
" any pixel being reported twice;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3114
msgid ""
"review the October alerts before the next run: an alert confirmed by then"
" can become the earlier loss that November's alerts grow from, and a "
"clearing that keeps growing shows its history in Analysis and in the "
"Overview;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3115
msgid ""
"check the questionnaire before splitting: a question added after the "
"packages are built needs **Regenerate packages**;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3116
msgid ""
"review the alerts still **Not reviewed** in the earlier sets too, since "
"the Overview's comparison is only as complete as the reviews behind it; "
"and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/modules/dwn/alert_module.rst:3117
msgid ""
"use **Duplicate** in the `Project <defo-project-duplicate_>`_ dialog to "
"monitor a neighbouring area with the same sources, mask and layers."
msgstr ""

